window.MSB=window.MSB||{};MSB["perl-en"]=[["The captivating saga of a pearl's making unfolds in the deepest depths of the ocean, where darkness wraps every living thing in a dim night. Here, on the floor of a boundless world of watery mysteries, the wondrous process of a pearl's birth begins.","It all starts with a tiny grain of sand. By chance it slips into the soft, sensitive heart of a mollusc. At first it is irritation, pain, nausea. The mollusc cannot escape it, and its only way out is to respond.","Protecting itself from the irritant, the mollusc secretes a beautiful, rare substance, building up layer upon layer of crystalline material around the grain of sand. Sometimes this response can take decades.","What happens in the heart of the mollusc is a true miracle. The feeling of nausea becomes a creative act of self-defence. An unfavourable circumstance becomes the embodiment of beauty and distinction.","After years and years of strenuous work, the mollusc turns a negative stimulus into a source of inner harmony and natural elegance. And at last, great hardship leads to the creation of a wonderful pearl. It is a moment of eternity, appearing before us in all its unrepeatable beauty.","There is something wonderfully symbolic in this process. It teaches us to see beauty even in the hardest circumstances, to turn challenges into opportunities and to believe that even the deepest darkness can hide the highest beauty.","Like these pearls, we are in a constant state of transformation. Like the grain of sand, negative situations and challenges can enter our lives. Sometimes it is loss, disappointment, hardship, or even physical and emotional pain.","This is the first step in forming a new pearl in our lives. Like the mollusc, we have a choice: we can let negative circumstances make us victims, or we can accept them as challenges that will help us become stronger and wiser.","Throughout life we build up our «layers of pearl»: the experience, skills and wisdom we gain. At every stage we have the opportunity to turn our inner life, even in the darkness of hardship, into something incredibly important and beautiful.","When this «pearl» finally appears in our lives, we can look at it with pride and deep gratitude. We understand that without those challenges, without the hurts and the high points, we would not be who we are now. We can see beauty and worth in our own growth and development.","So life is like the making of a pearl: it is not always an easy road, but it can always lead to an inner beauty and worth that are worth every hardship and obstacle we may meet along the way."],["All my life, amid a crowd of voices, I have heard many people say that everything that happens is decided beyond their control. They believe in «fate», which they are convinced does not depend on their own aspirations. This leads to an interest in horoscopes, belief in various superstitions and visits to fortune-tellers. People feel they have no control over their own lives and accept that their destinies are governed by unknown forces. So they try to uncover the secret of how to influence these forces and improve their lot. Even believers in God can convince themselves that He makes every decision about their future and that they have no free will or right to make their own decisions. But as a believer I want to stress that, although God has all power and might, from the very beginning He gave human beings a sovereign will to choose and make decisions at every step of their lives.","From the very beginning, from the days of Adam, God showed humankind that it has various possibilities for shaping its future and the right to choose, even when that choice is conditioned by outside influences. This story highlights the fact that a person is not simply an object of existence on which fate and decisions depend. People have their own sovereign will and can determine their own path, even in light of influences and circumstances. This ability to choose makes us active participants in shaping our own future.","«And the LORD God took the man, and put him into the garden of Eden to dress it and to keep it. 16 And the LORD God commanded the man, saying, Of every tree of the garden thou mayest freely eat: 17 But of the tree of the knowledge of good and evil, thou shalt not eat of it: for in the day that thou eatest thereof thou shalt surely die.» Genesis 2:15–17.","Although man made a fatal mistake and sinned, with consequences for all humanity to this day, the merciful God did not leave him alone before the endless trials of his lot. Instead, He offered His own way of deliverance and salvation. What gives each of us hope is the belief that even in hard moments of life, when we may feel alone before our challenges and our mistakes, there is a way to put things right and do better. God's love for us does not depend on our deeds or lost opportunities, and our right to free will remains unchanged throughout life. More than that, He is ready to become our partner in transforming our lives, if only we agree to heed the call to live by faith. He did not leave us helpless to grope our way through life. He gave us a handbook that serves as a reliable map through the tangled labyrinths of events. The Bible is a book that holds answers to every question, open to each and every person in every age. It lifts the veil of eternity and teaches the principles of success, helps us find harmony within and face the challenges without, making us people of success and progress. But like Adam, we have the ability to choose, and it is this ability that lays a great responsibility on us. Moses stressed this to a people who had just been freed from slavery and been given an extraordinary opportunity to shape their own future.","«I call heaven and earth to record this day against you, that I have set before you life and death, blessing and cursing: therefore choose life, that both thou and thy seed may live.» Deuteronomy 30:19.","Why does Moses call heaven and earth as witnesses that we have the right and the responsibility to choose? Because just like the endurance of the earth on which we walk, build our plans and work for our living, and the vastness of the sky under which we dream, think and place our hopes, these reflect our right to choose. This makes us neither victims of forces working in the shadows nor gods responsible for our own fate; it makes us free beings, who have the right to choose and can change their lives for the better. The story of the two generations who heard these words and witnessed Moses' speech shows us that every person has within them the ability to choose their path into the future and so to transform their life, becoming a better version of themselves where needed.","The wise King Solomon, who thought deeply about life, happiness, success and wisdom, observed:","«In all thy ways acknowledge him,","and he shall direct thy paths.» Proverbs 3:6.","He reminds us how important it is to remember the Lord: both as an invitation to use our right to choose in line with His best plans, and as a reminder that He is always ready to help us change ourselves and our lives for the better. It is an inspiration to believe and to move with purpose towards positive change. Our life is not only the point where we were born; it is the road we walk. A road always means a journey and the chance to discover something new; it lets us reach new places and change direction when needed. To «acknowledge» means to make our steps more aware and our life conscious. A conscious life will never say: «Nothing depends on me, I was born this way, it's my karma.» A conscious life will not agree to drift with the current; it puts its fins to work to swim upstream.","To make this more convincing, let us recall the Lord's words, which confirm that it is people themselves who choose their path; no one does it for them.","«Enter ye in at the strait gate: for wide is the gate, and broad is the way, that leadeth to destruction, and many there be which go in thereat:","Because strait is the gate, and narrow is the way, which leadeth unto life, and few there be that find it.» Matthew 7:13–14.","What can these words tell us? First, they remind us of our right to choose, even if we don't acknowledge it, and that the path of self-development and transformation can be hard. We understand this, and that is why most people choose the easier path: blaming fate and believing that nothing depends on them. But when we choose a conscious life and feel responsible for what happens in our inner world, we set out on the path of saving our own life. So the position that outside factors influence our lives more than we do becomes a convenient excuse for those who don't want to change anything in their inner world.","On this score I have both an unpleasant experience and evidence that changing your life is possible. For a time I was convinced that every person could change their life and, above all, wanted to, consciously or subconsciously. So I began actively promoting the idea of a new life among my acquaintances and people I had been friends with in the past. I met each of them and personally tried to get across that they could break away from an aimless life and begin discovering new opportunities. I even invested my own money to help them take a step of faith and start on a new road. Honestly, although I did it out of a cherished dream, I did not expect gratitude from them, only hoped for some response showing it had not all been in vain. Some treated me with contempt, some took offence, thinking I wanted to humiliate them, and some saw in it a secret wish of mine to manipulate and use them. For me it was a complete disappointment. All I wanted was to tell them: «Friends, my life has changed, and yours can change too if you want it to.» And the answer I got, in words or without them, was the question: «What do you want from me? Why do you keep pushing your ideas? Yes, maybe my life doesn't have much meaning, but I don't want to change anything.» So at a certain point I decided I would no longer try to influence other people's lives. I couldn't understand why none of those I approached showed the slightest interest in making their lives more conscious. But I was affected by other situations, which happened, as I thought, by chance. In different circumstances I met various businessmen who told me the same thing: «What I have and what I've achieved in recent years is all because I listened to your teaching. It changed my life, and I'm sincerely grateful to you for what you preach.» This inspired me greatly: change is possible, since even a businessman with undeniable success, living in full prosperity, slept in an ordinary garage when he started out because he had no home and not enough money. And even a man with four criminal convictions began a new life and changed so much that people who knew him could hardly recognise him. I heard many such stories, and they contained similar words and phrases, such as: «Pastor, I'm ready to go up on stage and tell everyone that it works!» And the point here is not me, but these people and the principles of the Bible they dared to apply.","So are we able to change? I'll be frank: no, it's impossible. A person is born the way they are, and nothing can affect that. Every attempt is just a waste of time and energy, so don't fool yourself. You were born with a certain set of qualities, a limit to your abilities and a certain measure of luck. Just as you can't change your sex, the colour of your eyes or your fingerprints, you can't be anyone other than who you are now. On the other hand, are we able to change? Yes, it is possible. We did not choose our sex or the circumstances in which we spent part of our life, and some things are beyond our power to change, but we have the right to choose, to be transformed, to change our life and our thoughts; we have the opportunity to become a new person. You'll ask me what all this means. And I'll answer: both options are true, and it is up to you to choose the answer that is true for you.","Asking whether a person can change themselves can indeed be an effective way to provoke thought and inspire reflection. In this way we get the chance to rethink our own beliefs and consider the possibility of positive change in our lives. Both options are true in the sense that whatever a person believes, they will hold to in their conviction. So I want to get across this thought: if a person believes it is impossible for them to change, it will stay that way until they abandon that point of view and believe it is possible.","Thinking that we will always stay as we are now is a mistaken judgement. What is our «self» made of? Partly, of course, of the natural traits we inherited at birth, which may not be changeable. But by better understanding the uniqueness of particular traits, we can look at ourselves, on the one hand accepting our uniqueness, and on the other understanding how this uniqueness may help or hinder us in reaching our goals. Most likely we are born with a certain set of qualities, such as temperament, a tendency to certain behaviour, special talents and character traits. But this is only part of who we are, and it does not determine a hundred per cent who we will become. Behind our natural traits stand many acquired ones, formed over the course of life. Our consciousness and our ability to learn and grow also shape our behaviour and achievements.","Yet not all the traits we have are built into us from birth. Most of them form over the course of our lives and become so much a part of our consciousness that we easily take them as part of ourselves. Telling these acquired traits from natural ones is very hard, because we have lived with them for a long time. They include our established habits, the knowledge we have gained over our lives, the information we have absorbed from various sources and the influence of our surroundings, which can shape our view of life. All these together make up our worldview and convictions. Our family and surroundings in childhood, the information we receive, the books we read or don't read, films, friends and acquaintances, even impressions we unconsciously absorb, past events: all these become our advisers in making decisions and shape our picture of the world. Even when a person tries to appear independent in their judgements, they are still influenced by what is already in their mind. That is why, often, when we make a decision or consider changing our life, we unconsciously replay old scenarios.","This is why life often seems to move in a circle, or rather in a spiral, where similar scenarios repeat again and again, only at different levels. Incidentally, this is exactly what can lead some people to believe that such things are their fate or the result of interference by unknown magical forces, and they may start looking for ways to lift this «curse». But is there a way out of this circle, or is everything destined to keep moving along a set trajectory?","If there were no way out, life would lose its meaning, and we would not be able to read this book together.","But changing your life is something more than just «on Monday I'll start a new life». We have had many such beginnings in our lives, and we have seen that in most cases they change nothing, and we remain the same people we were before. For change to happen, and for us to witness amazing transformations, a completely different level of effort is needed. First, it is important to realise that it really is possible and within your power. Second, you need to understand the principles by which it can be achieved. Sense your God-given consciousness, which rules over natural traits and acquired skills and is able to analyse how you make decisions. Then you will be able to ask yourself: Why do I think this way? Why do I make this decision every time? Where did I get the belief that I can't do this? Why do I do what I do and not something else? Try looking at your life from another point of view, as if observing from the outside: what would you say, what would you think? Here's a simple example: most of us know how to give others valuable, kind advice on how to act so that all goes well for them. In Soviet times there was a joke that the Soviet Union got its name because everybody loved giving everybody advice (sovet). But seriously, why are those who give everyone advice somehow unable to put their own lives in order? Because they see other people's lives clearly, but find it hard to assess their own critically and work out what needs to change. The saying comes to mind: «You can't see the wood for the trees.» To see the wood you have to step back, or better still climb a hill. Only then will the whole picture open up before you, and perhaps you will be able to spot the path you need, leading in the right direction. So where do you start, and what first steps should you take? Start by asking yourself healthy, constructive questions.","A member of a religious community goes to the head of the synagogue and asks: «Rabbi, I have a question that troubles me. Why did God create man?» The teacher replies: «Why do you need an answer when you have such a wonderful question?»","«Counsel in the heart of man is like deep water;","but a man of understanding will draw it out.» Proverbs 20:5.","Everything begins with awareness, and becoming aware of the right questions plays an important role. Questions help us challenge long-held beliefs and limits such as «I can't do it because I can't», «I'm not able to succeed because there have never been successful people in our family» or «I can't learn anything new; I'm already a fully formed person».","By asking ourselves honestly why we think this and whether the statement is true, we may conclude that, apart from justifying this position with the arguments we have always used, which have no solid basis and amount to «because it's always been that way», there are no objective grounds at all. This can inspire us to change our views and take steps towards transformation. It is as if you give yourself advice on how to change, the way you would advise someone else. So why does giving advice to others seem easier than doing it for ourselves? The main reason is that we see the other person from the outside and can view their situation more objectively, and above all we bear no personal responsibility for decisions that require crossing our own mental limits and excuses. You need to give yourself advice the way you would give it to someone else, because this is exactly what can help us transform our lives.","Understand one simple thing: all your skills, habits and character traits that have already become part of you were acquired over the course of your life. And if you have become who you are now, it happened through long practice of thinking in certain ways, taking in certain information and doing certain things again and again, until they became your habits. In the same way you can begin to master new thoughts, fill yourself with different information and introduce new habits. The result will be a change in the quality of your life and a deeper awareness of yourself. Everything we have now, and who we are, is the result of our past thoughts and beliefs. Our life is a reflection of our picture of the world, made up of different elements that we have acquired and built into our consciousness. If we manage to change this picture, to replace the mosaic with a different pattern, it will lead to change in the future.","But this can create a feeling that we are losing ourselves. How can we go on living without our usual doubts, when we are used to feeling sorry for ourselves or tasting the sweetness of being victims of others' indifference? How will we live without our «dear old selves», so used to failure and powerlessness? For a long time we will miss ourselves, so there will be a strong temptation to return to the familiar state and go on complaining about life. As the saying goes, «never part with your loved ones». So we need to stop cherishing our past self and learn to love ourselves in a new image, as a person in a new state. Love yourself as you have never yet been, completely new, the self you are creating now. When this happens, you will feel new potential opening up in your personality. And even if you still hear the whisper of the old «self», trying to tell you that you have betrayed «an old friend», «lost your real self» and that «none of this is real», with every step you will become more confident and decisive. If you have enough determination, motivation and faith, one day you will feel that just as you once felt natural in the image of your former «self», you now feel free in your new confidence and quality. But this is not the end of the road. You will discover a path that becomes a lifelong process, a constant discovery of your potential.","You have already tasted the sweetness of transformation, and it will forever become part of you. This part of you will keep moving you forward to new changes, transformations and victories."],["The chapter «The Cybernetics of Faith» looks at an important side of our psychological life: the influence of the goals held in our subconscious. Let's talk about how these goals shape our beliefs, actions and path in life.","The goals we set ourselves are not always obvious or conscious. Many of them are hidden in our subconscious, and we don't always understand why we act in certain ways or why we draw certain events into our lives. Yet these subconscious goals have a significant influence on our behaviour, choices and results. Our subconscious goals often shape our beliefs. For example, if you believe you don't deserve success, this may be linked to a subconscious goal of being a failure or unwanted. Our beliefs dictate how we see ourselves and the world. A subconscious goal can affect which events we draw into our lives. If your goal is to be happy, you are likely to attract events and opportunities that help you reach that state. Subconscious goals can affect our decisions and actions. If you have a goal of being recognised, you may seek out situations where you can get that recognition. Our goals affect how we see ourselves. If your goal is to be a good parent, you may see yourself as a caring and successful parent. Understanding your subconscious goals can help you change negative beliefs and strengthen positive ones. If you realise that you want to succeed, you can work on pushing away the negative beliefs that stand in the way of that goal. Examining subconscious goals develops self-awareness. It helps you understand yourself, your actions and your motivation better. Becoming aware of and analysing your subconscious goals can be a powerful tool for achieving the results you want in life and changing negative beliefs. You are free to shape your goals, and when they become conscious you gain more control over your life and the chance of greater happiness and success.","The title of this chapter, «The Cybernetics of Faith», may seem unexpected, but it reflects the deep connection between our beliefs, goals and psychological processes. Think of a plane taking off from the runway at, say, Berdychiv airport with the aim of landing at Kyiv airport. Its mission is to touch down at a particular place at a particular time, a matter of precision to within a few metres and seconds. But when the plane first starts its flight, its course is far from ideal; it is simply heading in the direction of Kyiv airport. During the flight, though, the plane uses navigation systems that constantly exchange information: where the plane is right now, what its speed and heading are and how closely it is keeping to the set course. With each exchange of data between the plane and its destination, the course is corrected. As the plane nears its target, its course becomes more and more accurate. In the end it lands exactly where it should, to within a few metres. This process, which I call the «cybernetics of faith», contains the idea of constant movement towards a goal even when we don't fully understand how to reach it. When we set out towards a goal, we usually don't have all the information we need or an exact plan. Many details remain unknown, but the main thing is to start.","In this process our actions may be imprecise at first, and we may come across many unclear things, skills and knowledge that we need to gain. But by holding on to our goal and direction, analysing our successes and shortcomings, we keep correcting our course and drawing closer to the goal. We learn along the way, and in the end this helps us achieve the result we want.","This cybernetics of faith shows that even when you don't know all the details of your path, it is important to believe in your goal and keep moving, steadily drawing closer to it.","At the very start it may simply be a desire to change your life, even when you don't know where to begin or which way to go. You may feel you lack experience and education, that it is hard to draw up a clear plan and set out its steps. But the most important things in this process are desire, motivation and faith. If you have a strong desire and believe in your abilities, you will gain all the knowledge and resources you need along the way. I always say that of two people, one with a good level of education, knowledge and resources but no strong desire or motivation, and the other perhaps without that education and those resources but with strong desire and faith, it is the second who will succeed. The first may not use their potential and may look for excuses for doing nothing, while the second will move mountains, learn and find the resources to reach the goal. They will pick up the missing skills as they move towards the goal, even if they make mistakes and stray off course from time to time.","«Cybernetics» is the study of systems, control and feedback. In the context of this chapter, «cybernetics» can refer to the processes of steering our goals and beliefs that take place in our subconscious. This cybernetics of faith moves us towards our goals, much as a plane is steered towards its set destination.","So let's first make sure we have enough desire to reach our goal and understand what exactly that goal is for us. Here's an example: almost everyone wants more love, success, money and confidence. As Mikhail Morgulis said, «you can never have too much love or money», and I have never met anyone who would refuse to live better. Yet many people subconsciously keep moving in the opposite direction. Why does this happen? Because they have a negative picture of the world. They are subconsciously afraid of having more success, money and responsibility. As we said, they are used to seeing themselves as failures and don't want to part with the familiar state of their soul. They may even show some interest in change and make attempts, but after the first setback they feel satisfied at having once again confirmed that they will remain victims. Every such attempt is for them a wait for proof that «they knew all along it wouldn't work». You will always hear something like: «We meant well, but it turned out as usual.» This can go on for quite a long time, until the person convinces themselves that all calls to change and all motivation to transform one's life are just a bluff with nothing to do with reality.","But there is another way: trying to understand why things happen the way they do and not otherwise. Becoming aware of and changing your picture of life, the goals of your subconscious.","For example, there are several symptoms showing that a person's picture of the world is not one that can inspire success and a healthy attitude to life. I'll give a few of them, drawing on the Bible, since this book contains all the information needed to change your life and achieve success:","«He that hasteth to be rich hath an evil eye,","and considereth not that poverty shall come upon him.» Proverbs 28:22.","Envy: is it the real cause of poverty and failure? Someone may ask how my thoughts affect my circumstances and what envy has to do with it. Envy is not a direct cause of a person's success or failure, but it can be an important signal of something deeper. It shows that a person may not believe in their own ability to succeed.","Envy can lead a person to start living other people's lives, comparing themselves with others. This can distort how they see themselves and their goals. They may set themselves tasks aimed not at their own happiness and personal success but at outdoing others. This can lead to wrong decisions and effort spent in the wrong direction.","So envy can be a sign that a person is not confident in their abilities, does not understand their own path to success and does not rate their strengths properly. It is important to understand this signal and channel its energy into building faith in yourself and consciously setting goals that lead to your own happiness and success, not simply to outdoing others.","But how can envy be recognised when a person may not even realise that it is envy influencing their thoughts and actions? Envy has its own marks, and here are a few. It often shows itself as criticism. People who criticise others' success often call it undeserved or gained by improper means. Such remarks may sound like this: «Look at that neighbour, he got all this only by stealing; an honest person can't afford such expensive property», «That person doesn't deserve what he has. I'm more decent, honest and intelligent, and all this should have been mine», or «So what if they're so „cool“? It doesn't make them smarter or better.» Every such criticism, every desire to belittle others or remark that their achievements are the result of dishonesty, is a sign of envy.","Or trying to outdo others in showing off your success. If the neighbour bought a new car, I must buy the same one, even if it means using financial reserves that could be better spent another way. The main goal is «to show everyone we can be cool too», but most often this brings neither joy nor a sense of success. «No worse than the neighbours» is a very poor motivator, because it can lead to inappropriate, unwise decisions that turn out to be costly in the long run.","How do you deal with envy if it is there? First, honestly admit to yourself that you feel envy. Second, understand that other people's success is no threat to your own dignity or your chance to succeed. Third, there will always be someone better off or worse off than you, and that is perfectly normal. What matters is being able to meet your needs and fulfil your potential. Fourth, everyone is given their own time and their own path to success. Finally, let others' success motivate you to become better in your work and your life. So envy is a poor adviser. You need to get rid of it as soon as possible by changing your picture of the world. You are a unique person with your own unique abilities and talents, so comparing yourself with others makes no sense. Your dignity does not depend on social status or other people's recognition. Success is not measured only by material well-being. Doing what you love, having the support of those around you and doing your work: these are the marks of a successful person. Better to be the best version of yourself than a poor copy of someone else.","«Listen, you devote all your time to money. Are you sure you don't want to live for what you really love?» «Yes, but I do love money.»","Here is another example of a false picture of the world that can govern a person at the subconscious level and lead not to success but, on the contrary, to poverty:","«There is that scattereth, and yet increaseth;","and there is that withholdeth more than is meet, but it tendeth to poverty.» Proverbs 11:24.","These words of the Bible may seem contradictory, since it looks as though the generous person should lose and the thrifty one should keep. But in fact this is a paradox. A paradox is something that at first glance contradicts itself but becomes clear at another level of understanding. This is why generosity is a spiritual law, which says that when we are generous it comes back to us with profit. It is a principle we find in the Bible. To be a generous person, you need faith that there will always be plenty and success, and no fear of letting go. Such a person does not live in fear; they have a healthy picture of the world, are always ready to see opportunities and take a creative approach to life. In the other example, the person who is excessively thrifty may be acting out of fear and a lack of faith that opportunities for success will come. Such a person focuses on protecting and keeping what they already have, for lack of faith that opportunities can grow. Thrift is certainly important and, as the Bible says, even recommended, since it helps achieve financial well-being. But it is important to tell normal thrift from its excessive form. In practice no one has become rich simply by economising on everything without a sensible strategy and faith in their own abilities. The only way to keep what you have is to multiply it. You can only multiply when you sow. To sow means to invest in your growth, your education and the improvement of your work so as to become even more effective. But it is even more important to be a sower, a person who sees their role as a channel of blessing for others and not only a reservoir for themselves. The law of nature reflects this principle too: what you sow will grow. So the law of sowing and reaping also works in spiritual life. Believers know this law well and keep seeing it at work in their lives when they follow its principles.","Don't close the doors of opportunity on yourself out of fear and the belief that you will have no chance of success. Believe in constant growth, and keep an open mind to new ideas and opportunities. Let your spiritual and emotional state be full of faith, energy and motivation for success. Then you will be able to see opportunities.","Let's talk about a few more key features of the human subconscious that can become obstacles on the road to success.","«Labour not to be rich:","cease from thine own wisdom.","Wilt thou set thine eyes upon that which is not?","for riches certainly make themselves wings; they fly away as an eagle toward heaven.» Proverbs 23:4–5.","Why does the Bible, which contains so much valuable advice and truth about how a person can become successful, say something that at first glance may seem to contradict the desire to succeed? After all, we know that a person can become successful, or rich for example, only if they are focused on reaching their goal. How are we to understand this important instruction? Let's try to understand the meaning better. First, the Bible does not reject the desire to succeed or to gain great wealth. On the contrary, in these words we can see a warning not to make wealth the main goal, because it can get in the way of reaching other goals.","Second, the main, key message of these words is that if a person is too focused on gaining wealth alone and makes it their main goal, it can complicate their path in life and lead to losing the very thing they want to achieve. The Bible repeatedly stresses that the main goal of a successful person should be fulfilling their potential, expressing who they are in work that becomes their life's calling. Such a mission not only makes a person successful but also brings blessing to others who enjoy the fruit of their labour. For the person themselves it brings the desired result: achievements and satisfaction in the work they have chosen to do.","From the examples above we can see that in every case people aimed to improve their lives and become more successful, but it either didn't work or led to the opposite result. This happened because there was a wrong picture of the world in their subconscious.","This is seen when a person strives for success while believing that success is a bad thing and money is evil. As a result, all their attempts to reach the goal end in failure. Their subconscious holds the message: «You are forbidden to succeed, because it is wrong.»","One last example: success always means not only greater prosperity, opportunity and higher status but also greater responsibility and accepting certain risks. So a person who is subconsciously set on avoiding responsibility in life will unconsciously sabotage their own success. Such a person may be highly motivated and creative at the stage of planning a project and preparing to carry it out. They may work very hard towards their goal throughout the process, but at the last stage, for example when contracts need signing, resources need investing or responsibility for the venture must be taken, they may lose interest or put the moment off. They may change their mind at the last minute, be late for the signing, suddenly feel unwell or find creative ways to avoid the final stage. So despite wanting all the trappings of success, they are not ready to leave their comfort zone, where they feel safe and carry no responsibility.","What matters here is genuine faith: faith not in what a person is trying to do but in what they truly believe.","You know what it's like to get behind the wheel every day to drive to work or the office. The process has become so familiar that it runs almost automatically. You get into the car and set off. During the drive you may be lost in your thoughts and plans, listening to an audiobook or the news. Your body and attention respond to the road automatically: stopping at red lights and turning the right way at junctions. And since your office is outside the city and the journey is long, you have time to pray, talk on the phone and remind yourself of the important things you need to do that day. Getting from point A to point B, you are hardly aware of the process; it all happens automatically. Even when there are traffic jams, you almost automatically find another route to get around them and reach your destination faster. Why does this happen? Because your subconscious already holds a clear goal: reaching your destination. In the same way, in matters of success we move towards our main goal regardless of what we are busy with at the moment or what tasks are in front of us.","Now imagine another scenario: you become aware of your desires and set yourself a real goal that inspires you. You clearly define point B, where you need to end up, and start moving. Even if a lot lies unknown ahead, or the route gets complicated and at times you don't know what to do, your subconscious guides you in the right direction, constantly keeping before you the place where you need to arrive.","Even if you have to take a new route and don't have enough information, or unknown places lie along the way, you are still able to travel that road, because you know you will find solutions and the right answers along the way. Even if at first you are not aware of the full complexity of the process and the challenges that may await you.","The Bible contains the remarkable story of Abraham, a true hero of faith. His journey began when he received God's call to leave his home and set out for an unknown land that he was to inherit. The Bible tells us that Abraham set out without knowing the exact direction of his future. But even then he had a clear goal. Along the way more and more was revealed to him, and God showed him the land that, by promise, became his inheritance.","At times Abraham made mistakes and strayed from his route, but his determination and faith in the goal kept him headed the right way. In time he received new revelation: the promise of the birth of an heir and of becoming the father of a great nation. And the story culminated in God revealing to Abraham that through his descendants the Messiah would come and save humanity from sin. Abraham's cybernetics of faith inspires us to believe in our goals and our future.","Don't let the unknown frighten you or stop you from starting on your way. The first steps may feel uncertain, but it is through them that you move forward. Along the way you will gain the skills you need, pick up the necessary knowledge and find the route when you need it. The main thing is to start, believe in yourself and not doubt.","Don't let your doubts and excuses, including the fact that you've never done this before, convince you. We were born into this world with no experience or understanding, yet we managed to grow up and reach adulthood. Knowledge is gained gradually, and the doors to it open gradually. In the same way, success comes to those who carry within them the goal of fulfilling their potential and living life as it is. Let's repair our core settings and expose all the inner contradictions that stop us reaching the goal we want. Let's define the picture we need and start working to make it real. You should already begin to feel like the person you dream of becoming, and to see yourself where you want to be.","How to reach your goal is a secondary question. The main thing is to have a goal and enough motivation. Everything else will come about through the «cybernetics of faith», if you truly want it."],["It all begins with dissatisfaction. It may be dissatisfaction with your life, your finances or the lack of meaning in what you do. It is that unpleasant feeling when you realise the days are flying by and nothing real seems to be happening in your life; there is no true meaning. At the same time you watch other people's lives looking brighter, like a cruise ship from which festive music drifts and the voices of holidaymakers can be heard celebrating life. The ship, lit up with bright lights, sails past a poor village whose people have never known anything but hard work. They can only watch as others live in a world of happiness and fulfilled dreams. And there, in the darkness of night, someone looks at that glow and feels an emptiness in their heart, because it seems they will never have what those people enjoying the party have.","It is a very painful, sad feeling. But sometimes this pain can hold within it the birth of new life and hope. This pain can be the beginning of a new and precious pearl.","Somewhere deep in the heart a desire for transformation is born, a resolve not to accept the way things are, not to admit that existence is powerless, and to fight for your own future. A fight for your own happiness and the meaning of life. This fight already makes us true human beings, living with purpose and meaning, and it is worth every moment, whatever its outcome.","This pain is a necessary condition for new life to begin, since the new can only be born out of the pain of the old world being torn down. I don't mean physical pain or suffering, but a mixture of doubt that is a necessary part of the longing for change and transformation. It is the doubt that the old order of things can still satisfy our longing for a full life. The second part of this mixture is the breaking down of old habits and approaches to life and the grafting in of new patterns of thought and behaviour, which can be painful.","«For godly sorrow worketh repentance to salvation not to be repented of: but the sorrow of the world worketh death.» 2 Corinthians 7:10.","This sorrow and pain do us no harm; they are different from ordinary sadness. It is exactly the sorrow that leads to «repentance», a word that comes from Greek and means a change of mind, a complete reversal in life and a change of direction. So when you have long been heading in one direction, repentance means that at some point you realise this course was wrong, and your thinking is completely turned over. After that you turn around to move in a completely different direction.","Without this kind of «repentance», change in life becomes impossible. The new is not just an add-on to the old; it is a complete change of everything that exists.","The process of repentance is beautifully shown in the Gospel parable of the prodigal son. It is the moment of becoming aware of your miserable existence, when catharsis comes, the moment of truth, and you say to yourself: «What am I doing here, in this wilderness, far from what really belongs to me, far from my father's house?» Realising at that moment that you are your father's son and he has something better for you becomes the turning point of your life. The same happens to those who understand that our Heavenly Father, whose children we are, has something far better for us than what is happening to us. That sorrow stirred in him the resolve to change his life and choose another path. In time this resolve brought the prodigal son to a place of joy and plenty.","Repentance is quite a radical step. As long as we are willing to put up with the old state of affairs and find it acceptable, nothing will change. We may try to improve the situation. But when a decisive desire arises to be rid of the old and gain the new, we become ready for decisive action. You can't jump 98 per cent of the way across a chasm, or be half pregnant. Either it happens a hundred per cent or it doesn't. Either we make the decision and it takes hold of us completely, or we stay in the old state; there is no middle ground.","All these processes take place deep within us, and they can be compared to an incubation process, like the moment a man's seed meets a woman's egg, or a pearl grows inside a mollusc. A new idea, a new vision, a new picture of the world acts on our heart, starting a process like conception, development and growth, right up to the moment when a new concept of life comes into the world. The incubation can be slow, starting with dissatisfaction with the old state of things, then conception by the idea of a new world and gradual development. It takes time, as the «new» gradually takes up more and more room, pushing out the old. The birth, or appearing, of the new happens when a new picture of the world is formed, when you understand what you want and which way you want to go.","«And he said, So is the kingdom of God, as if a man should cast seed into the ground;","And should sleep, and rise night and day, and the seed should spring and grow up, he knoweth not how.","For the earth bringeth forth fruit of herself; first the blade, then the ear, after that the full corn in the ear.","But when the fruit is brought forth, immediately he putteth in the sickle, because the harvest is come.» Mark 4:26–29.","Have you seen how a pregnant woman changes, in her look and her behaviour? It seems the same thing happens to a person when the idea of a new life is born in them, a concept that changes under the influence of inner processes. They realise there is something inside that neither they nor others can see yet, but in time it will begin to show. So once an idea has been conceived, we carry within us projects, creative plans and future discoveries that will wait for their time to be realised. Now our life no longer belongs to us alone; it serves a great mission bigger than ourselves. We begin to dream and imagine how this mission will take shape in reality, how we will see it with our own eyes. For now it lives only in our heart and imagination, in quiet secrecy. It is a process of inner growth and formation that happens without noise or fuss. That is why there is a folk belief that «you shouldn't tell everyone your plans, or they may not come true». We may not believe in folk superstitions, but there is wisdom in this idea. This process welcomes silence, secrecy and inner attention.","By telling others your plans and what is happening in your inner world, it is almost as if you scatter the energy. This may seem strange, since you are trying to put a deep and complex process into words and share it. At that moment the process becomes simplified, less deep and less inspiring for you yourself. Doing this all the time is like constantly taking the grain out of the mollusc's shell to show others: it can stop its natural growth. Besides, other people who find it hard to grasp your feelings and faith may even clip the wings of your vision. Keep your dream secret. Live this goal inwardly, working on it through prayer, reflection, study, searching for the information you need and your own labour towards it. You are constantly preparing yourself for the moment when the time comes for this project to be realised. Yet you are not waiting for it all to happen by itself; for you it has already happened, in the depths of your heart. So you have become the bearer of a new life that demands a complete transformation of who you are.","«Being pregnant with an idea, a concept or a transformation of character» is used metaphorically and means that a person feels within themselves the potential for change and growth.","Being pregnant with an idea means carrying within you a concept or a dream of something new and significant. It is like how a pregnancy carries a potential new life. An idea can bring a new project, direction or achievement into the world. At first the idea may not be fully formed, without a clear sense of how it might look in the end. But the more attention we give it and the more we study it, the clearer it becomes and the better we understand what steps are needed to bring it about. It shows that you are actively developing the idea, working on it and ready to put all your effort into making it real, just as pregnancy requires care and support for new life to grow and develop. Being pregnant with a transformation of character means being ready to change yourself, your state and your approach to life in order to achieve something new and better. It points to an inner transformation, like the way pregnancy transforms a woman's body for the birth of a child. But sadly, not all the ideas and potential for change that sink into people's hearts over their lives get the chance to see the light. Most remain unused, and sometimes they die without even reaching the stage of conception. Many ideas that come to people's minds are immediately dismissed through inattention, when a person gives no time to their spiritual and personal growth. Others stay at the stage of thinking and never turn into action, or are judged too unrealistic. How many times have we met people with countless creative ideas who have never made a single one real? Perhaps we ourselves know the feeling: an idea, a project or something significant is born. At first it seems brilliant to us, but over time it goes unrealised. And when we see someone else carry out what was once «our idea», we feel we have lost the chance to be first. This shows that the concept found its way into our heart, but we did not nurture it. Someone else, receiving the same idea, managed to turn it into reality.","This is an important lesson I have learned: to pay attention to every thought born in my heart. Even if it seems unrealistic, even if no one has tried to carry it out before. Better that I try and make a mistake than throw it out without trying. To sense whether an idea is viable, you have to try to bring your plan to life. Success is not always the first attempt. Often success is the result of one good attempt among many failed ones.","I don't know anyone who doesn't know what a dream is. Almost everyone in the world dreams of something in their life. But often the dreams that arise when we are young gradually fade over time. Remember how students and schoolchildren talk about their ambitions? Some dream of becoming politicians, outstanding public figures or famous musicians who will write and perform well-known pieces. But why do some of them disappear from that field once they turn thirty? Why do some prefer pragmatic things and justify it by saying «life isn't always the way you imagine it; you have to think about real things»? Over time some people may lose the ability to dream altogether. Then they start insisting that «dreams are just illusions, emptiness; they too once dreamed of many things, but it made no difference to their lives». But have you ever wondered why God gave people the ability to dream? Not so that we would simply dismiss our dreams as a distraction from real life. The true meaning of dreams is that they inspire us, let us glimpse a possible scenario for our life and reveal potential that may be hidden within us. Dreams are, so to speak, the language of faith. They let us look at a possibility and say: «Look, this could happen in your life; it is within reach.» When we talk about dreams, we mean the real language of the spirit, not childish fantasies like «may a suitcase of money fall from the sky at my feet», although, to be honest, that wouldn't be bad. All inventors are dreamers; all business pioneers are dreamers. Creativity is not limited to musicians and artists. Creativity is present wherever there is movement and discovery.","If a person throws away their dreams and their belief in their own good fortune, they will be forced to watch the drive and initiative of others and become their satellite, instead of creating their own orbit and drawing closer to fulfilling their own potential. It is life on the shore, a life of watching rather than taking part in active creation. It's like listening to Luciano Pavarotti over the phone while a friend hums him down the line to you. «Very interesting, but I can't make any of it out.»","Over time many of us may lose the ability to dream. «I'm too old to dream», «the kids, the household, the cat, the dog and everything else: where's the room for dreaming?» But as they say, «winter is no obstacle to hockey.» At any age and in any circumstances there is always room for dreams and hopes to awaken.","Let me share a story from the Bible with you. When Abraham first believed the Lord, he was a mere 75 years old. Not a bad age to start a new life. In time he gave himself to the dream he had received from God: to have a son. Usually at that age people think least of all about having a child and are interested in other sides of life instead.","Abraham stood out from everyone. He was pregnant with the idea of the promised land and the birth of his son. It is no accident that it is written: «Abraham begat Isaac.» It was the birth of his dream, which became reality. Yet, as with each of us, time flew by, and Abraham remained childless. He was 99 when he decided to let go of the dream: «Well, that's life. Perhaps it's time to accept that my dream won't come true.» So he turned to God and said: «Let my servant be my heir.» He hoped God would understand him and say: «Abraham, I understand you; you believed as best you could, but let's be realistic. You're not young any more, and perhaps it's too hard.» But God contradicted Abraham and stressed that the dream he had carried in his heart for 25 years must come true and that he should not give it up. And in time Abraham held his son in his arms.","«And he brought him forth abroad, and said, Look now toward heaven, and tell the stars, if thou be able to number them: and he said unto him, So shall thy seed be. And he believed in the LORD; and he counted it to him for righteousness.» Genesis 15:5–6.","Imagine an old man to whom the Lord says: «Look at the stars and count them; that is how many children you will have.» It seems to me that the greatest dreamer in the world is God Himself. The stars Abraham saw were not Abraham's dream but God's dream, which He wanted to pass on to Abraham. The «stars» we see with the eyes of our heart are not our dreams either; they are the dreams of our Creator, who wants to pass them on to us. So the question is: are you ready to receive this seed into your heart and make God's dreams a reality in your life?"],["Imagine that one fine day you decide to become the person you have always dreamed of being. You want to set off on a new road and discover your new «self». But for that you need the courage to show yourself in a new light, especially to those who know you well. What's the big deal, you might think? Yet it is not an easy step.","Those who think they «know you like the back of their hand» have already formed an opinion about your abilities and limits. These ideas may be positive, but they always have a frame, limited by what people have already seen or perceived. They are based on your past actions but take no account of the potential hidden deep within you.","So when a person tries to change, to travel the road to their dreams and self-improvement, they inevitably meet scepticism and even resistance from those around them. And the greatest challenge is when the people closest to them take this attitude.","«A prophet is not without honour, save in his own country, and in his own house.» Matthew 13:57.","«A prophet is not without honour, save in his own country, and in his own house.» Why does this happen? Because a person who until a certain moment was just «one of us» suddenly becomes someone with a special message. This transformation, this shift from «ordinary» to «exceptional», is often a shock for those used to seeing them in only one image.","It is hard for those around to accept that someone they knew as simple and unremarkable might have something deep and important to say to the world. Not because they don't wish them well, but because their ideas about them are already set.","Such a person may find it much easier to open up to strangers, who see them without preconceptions. Strangers can take them as they are now, without comparisons with the past.","But do you really need to change your surroundings or move somewhere else to begin a new stage of life? Not necessarily. But you must understand that, faced with misunderstanding and doubt from those around you, you will need enough inner strength and confidence to keep going, believing in yourself and your calling.","«A man's foes shall be they of his own household.» Matthew 10:36.","At first glance this phrase may seem contradictory, given the Bible's central command to love your neighbour. But looking deeper into the context, we can see that it contains a great truth.","The point of the phrase is not to portray loved ones as enemies in the literal sense, but that they are the ones who have the greatest influence on us. They share life's joys and hardships with us, and their attitude and opinion can affect our decisions more than we imagine.","Well-meant advice and warnings from loved ones, though they come from the best intentions, can sometimes end up limiting our possibilities. Fear of the new, a desire to «protect» us from possible mistakes or setbacks, can lead us to start doubting ourselves.","Such moments show how important it is to have inner strength and faith in yourself to go your own way, whatever others think. It is important to try to understand the thoughts and fears of those close to us, while keeping our individuality and following our inner voice.","So «a man's foes shall be they of his own household» may not mean open conflict, but the phrase reminds us that life's greatest challenge is finding a balance between being true to yourself and wanting to be understood and accepted by those around you.","Sometimes those closest to us don't understand us straight away. Their recognition and support may come not at once but after a long time. And this period of waiting can be a real trial, because it hurts most when those dearest to us don't see or value our efforts, dreams and aspirations.","This time is our probation, when we overcome obstacles and face doubts and perhaps even our own fears. But it is in such moments that we grow and gain strength and self-confidence.","At this time it is important to keep faith in yourself and be honest with yourself about your desires and dreams. This will help you not to lose your way or stop halfway to your goal. Remember that every step, even if it seems small or unsuccessful, brings us closer to the final goal.","In time, when the fruit of our efforts becomes obvious and our loved ones see how we have changed and what we have achieved, their recognition and support will come. Until then we need patience and faith in ourselves, and must not stop on the road to our dream.","When we make a choice in the direction of our aspirations and start acting, our life begins to change. These changes are inevitable and often become noticeable not only to us but to others. Our appearance may be refreshed, we may take up new activities, discovering new horizons and interests. Our values and priorities may also be rethought, since we now see the world with different eyes.","But these changes may bring a number of challenges with them. People used to seeing us a certain way may not immediately understand and accept our new image, our new goals and aspirations. It is in such moments that it is important to stay true to yourself, your inner voice and your vision of the future.","Don't let the past keep you in chains. Try not to look back with nostalgia or sadness. Instead, live for the future, stay devoted to your intentions and act decisively on the way to your dream. Believe in yourself, and don't be afraid to become who you really want to be.","Transformation begins on the inside, with your inner convictions. If before you were troubled by low self-esteem and a lack of faith in yourself, over time you begin to value yourself more. Where there used to be heaviness and a constant search for others' approval, now confidence in your own strength and decisions appears. This cannot help but show in your appearance.","A person who knows where they are going, has a clear vision of their goals and believes they will reach them, always looks confident. You can sense their confidence even without knowing them personally: free movements, a confident posture, a direct gaze. Such a person's energy is full of purpose. By contrast, an insecure person cannot hide their confusion, and others sense it in their look, movements, voice and expression. Our inner steadiness and conviction always show on the outside.","The same applies to a person's outward appearance, the image they create for themselves. If someone has lost interest in life, it often shows in how they look: they become less well-groomed and stop giving themselves the attention they once did. They seem not to care how they look to the world. And although clothes don't always reflect a person's finances, they always reveal their inner world. It's not about how much things cost but about what a person chooses for themselves. Your clothes are a calling card that displays your goals, intentions and ambitions.","So your inner transformation will certainly affect your outward appearance. Don't convince yourself that it doesn't matter, as if only what is inside counts. Your inner world and inner qualities show in how carefully you treat yourself. Interest in life always goes hand in hand with the desire to do everything better: choosing neat clothes, keeping certain standards, taking care of yourself on every level.","Throughout human history, special attention has been paid to the importance of a person's inner and outer well-being. Even the Bible speaks of this harmony. In particular, it calls:","«to comfort all that mourn; to appoint unto them that mourn in Zion, to give unto them beauty for ashes, the oil of joy for mourning, the garment of praise for the spirit of heaviness.» Isaiah 61:2–3.","This quotation stresses the importance of caring not only for the state of the soul but also for one's appearance, as a reflection of inner harmony.","Some of you may be surprised that in a book about inner transformation I dwell on such seemingly «secondary things» as appearance. But I am convinced of the importance of image, because it plays a key role in how we feel and how others see us. A vivid example for me is Dr Bill Bassansky. I have never seen him looking untidy. Even after a long flight from the United States to Ukraine, he always looked impeccable.","I remember one occasion during our travels around Ukraine. We had to set off at six in the morning. I was so tired after the day that I didn't care at all how I looked; I just wanted to rest. Suddenly I heard a knock at the door. I thought it was just a dream, but when the knocking grew more real, I opened the door. There stood Bill: perfectly dressed, shaved, his hair neatly combed. He had a cup of coffee in his hands, and he said with a smile: «Good morning. I was praying today, and Jesus sent me a message: tell Dima Mason that I love him very much.»","For me this was clear confirmation that our appearance and our inner energy are closely connected. Bill showed me that neatness and attention to detail reflect our inner attitude to ourselves and to the world.","When we talk about the «cybernetics of our faith» and the transformation of character, we cannot leave out appearance. It is a mirror of our views and intentions. There is a well-known principle: «Create your image, and it will pave the way for you.» This should be understood as a call to become today the person you have always dreamed of being.","Yet, coming back to the main point of this chapter, for many people such a transformation may seem a challenge. That's because those around us, and sometimes we ourselves, are used to seeing us in a certain image. When that image starts to change, others are bound to react. You may feel you are being too bold in your new look.","The task is to boldly live out your vision of yourself. This is your way of self-expression, where you don't need to justify yourself. Every time people look at you, they should see your inner self saying: «Good day, it's me, the new me. The person you knew yesterday is in the past. Today I am a new person, transformed by divine love.»","Yes, this may take courage, but it is through this courage that you will be able to feel real, alive and unrivalled. Because this is your life, and only you can decide who you want to be.","Being like everyone else is a betrayal of yourself. Imagine a world where each of us is a copy of the others: the same thoughts, style and interests. Total uniformity. How long would it take for such a world to become boring? My answer: very quickly. There is an unwritten agreement not to stand out from the crowd and to make sure you don't cross some invisible boundaries of «normality».","Boldness is often misunderstood. If you allow yourself more than others do, you often hear reproaches: «Who do you think you are?» But the real question is different: why not let yourself be fulfilled, if others don't dare take the step?","Most people choose a limited life for fear of judgement. But your boldness, your desire to live to the full, can be a spark for others. Let your life be a bright example for those looking for the way to themselves. Live a full life, be yourself and inspire others to do the same.","Many of us constantly live in a world of «someday», putting off our real life until later. We imagine that one day the perfect moment will come, when circumstances are favourable, worries vanish and dreams come true. But the truth is that there is no perfect moment. It will not arrive automatically in the future; you create it here and now.","Life is not a rehearsal or a warm-up for some great event. It is the only performance we are given to play, and it is happening right before our eyes every day. Every moment, every action, every hesitation shapes our future.","Don't wait for the «perfect» moment, because it may never come. If you long for change and to reach your dreams and goals, do it now. It is in this moment that your greatest strength lies, and your chance to create the life you have always wanted.","There are moments in life when it seems that everything around us is shrouded in a fog of disappointment and grief. These moments can be compared to the ashes left after a fire: cold, colourless, lifeless. But there is a promise that lets us look at life differently. God promises to replace these ashes with a crown of glory, a symbol of victory, achievement and renewal.","The words «spirit of heaviness» describe a state of indifference and weariness, when the world around loses its colour. But instead of this dull covering comes the promise of a garment of glory. A new mood, new energy, a new outlook on life.","Looking around, it is easy to see people who seem worn out by life. Their world has gone pale, and there is no spark in their eyes. This is an important moment for change. Change your inner and outer world, get rid of whatever drags you down and let the new fill your heart.","So don't hold on to the past, and don't let old things and relationships stop you from moving forward. Get rid of what you don't need, embrace the new and live life to the full. You are worth it, and much more awaits you!","«Don't be so surprised: you are seeing me for the first time.» This applies first of all to ourselves. Sometimes we get so tangled in the routine of our habits, beliefs and stereotypes that we forget to look at ourselves without prejudice. We fail to notice our inner beauty, don't sense our hidden desires and certainly don't grasp the full depth of who we are.","Try throwing away all the templates imposed by society and look at yourself as a new, unexplored person. Find in yourself what makes you unique and what you want to develop. Give yourself the chance to open up to the world in a new way, as though you really were seeing yourself for the first time.","This new view of yourself may be a little shocking, but also very liberating. By recognising the unknown within you, you can give yourself new opportunities, new prospects and new horizons. So allow yourself to say: «Don't be surprised; today you are seeing yourself for the first time.» And discover a whole new world in who you are."],["«He that walketh with wise men shall be wise:","but a companion of fools shall be destroyed.» Proverbs 13:20.","We often think we choose our own surroundings: friends, colleagues, neighbours. We think we have full control over who is near us and that these choices reflect our free will. But is that really so?","Every choice we make reflects our inner beliefs, values and attitude to the world. And when we choose certain surroundings, we quietly send signals into the world about who we are. These signals don't go unnoticed. People with similar beliefs, thoughts and interests respond to them and come into our lives.","So the choice is partly an illusion: by choosing certain surroundings, we in effect set up a beacon that draws certain people to us. They sense that we are like them, that we understand them and can share common ideas and values.","But there is another side to the coin. Sometimes we choose surroundings that don't reflect our true values but are dictated by outside circumstances, social pressure or inner doubts. Then we risk ending up among people who don't share our convictions and may even lead us in the wrong direction.","So it is always worth asking yourself: Why did I choose these surroundings? What do they say about me? And do they really reflect my true «self»?","Remember that your surroundings are a mirror of your soul. Our surroundings are not simply the people near us; they are the sum of the energies, thoughts, emotions and relationships we choose in life. They are a web of connections that strongly influences how we see the world, our ambitions and our possibilities.","Our surroundings can set «markers», or limits. These limits are often invisible, but they narrow our view of the world, our actions and decisions. Through such «markers» we can end up in a «bubble», where our possibilities are limited to what we see around us.","Our surroundings, like a lift, can take us up or bring us down. Choosing the right «lift» can be the key to reaching our dreams and ambitions. It is the environment in which we absorb other people's words, thoughts, moods and energy.","Some people in our lives can drain our energy. After spending time with them we often feel tired, irritable or pessimistic. They seem to suck the life out of us, leaving emptiness behind.","On the other hand, there are people who inspire us, who make us feel joy, hope and enthusiasm. They give us faith in ourselves and open new horizons and opportunities. With them we feel capable of great things.","So it is very important to choose your surroundings carefully and consciously. They should be in harmony with our goals, dreams and beliefs. This is the key to inner peace, growth and success in life.","How do we choose our surroundings? It's the magnet of likeness.","Human beings are social creatures; our nature always longs for company and community. Yet we don't always think about how and why we choose our surroundings. Why are we drawn to these particular people? What makes them special to us?","The answer may lie in our subconscious needs and desires. We want to find common ground with those around us, to understand and be understood. And it is not always about physical or outward similarity; it is about inner vibrations, emotional resonance, shared values and interests.","Imagine a city with millions of people. In it live two people who have never seen each other but share the same passion for polar penguins. How will these two find each other among so many others? It's like a needle in a haystack, but the real wonder is that they really can meet!","Perhaps they will go to an exhibition about the polar regions, or meet in a library looking for a book about penguins. And when they discover their shared interest, a special connection will form between them. This invisible thread that links them is not just a shared interest; it is a sense of belonging, understanding and mutual support.","We attract what we focus our attention on, what we give our energy to. And when we follow our interests and find people who share our passions, our world becomes brighter, richer and more harmonious.","But there is also a dark side to our surroundings: when pain becomes the reflection of the soul.","It might seem that the world around us is simply a mirror of the world within. But what do we do when this mirror reflects the dark corners of the soul, painful wounds and secret fears? When the friends we choose to spend time with reflect not the best period of our life?","We have all faced moments when life turns into a crisis. At such times it may seem easiest simply to turn away from problems and seek oblivion in the company of those who don't judge or condemn. But is such company always support? Often, beneath a mask of indifference, lie one's own pain and the demons each of us battles on our way.","When we spend time with people who have a negative outlook or harmful habits, we can blind ourselves to our own problems. Shared experience can create an illusion of empathy, but by running away from our own painful thoughts we only deepen our wounds and lose the chance to heal.","So each of us must understand that by choosing our surroundings, we choose the path of our journey. If all we see in our friends is a reflection of our own painful wounds, it is time to consider whether it is time to change course. Each of us has the power to choose our future rather than let the past hold us captive.","By choosing our surroundings, we choose our future.","Every day we make choices. What to wear, what to eat, which way to go to work. But there is another choice on which far more depends: the choice of our surroundings.","The world around us is not just a neutral canvas; it shapes our future and how we see ourselves and life as a whole. And if we choose surroundings that breathe positivity, that want to grow, overcome obstacles and reach for new heights, that atmosphere is contagious. We begin to think and act the same way. We strive to become the best version of ourselves.","But a question may arise here: «How can I get into such surroundings when I feel such a big gap between myself and these „bright“ people?» The thing is, mixing with successful, positive people doesn't have to depend on material position or social status. What unites us is not the number of zeros in a bank account but shared values, goals and vision of the world.","There are countless communities, churches, interest clubs, workshops and conferences where you can meet like-minded people. Yes, at first it may feel a little awkward or unfamiliar. But it is important to realise that these people also once took this step, leaving their comfort zone in search of new horizons.","So choose your surroundings wisely. Choose your future. Let the people you spend time with become the lanterns that light your way to a happy, harmonious life.","Sometimes we think that successful people live in a world of their own, far from ordinary mortals. But the truth is that, like us, they value sincerity, openness and true values.","My story of meeting Dr Bill Bassansky is a vivid example. I was not well known, and my church was not big, but my faith was real. My desire to meet Dr Bill did not come from a wish for popularity or any kind of benefit. I was drawn to his wisdom, his outlook on life and his experience.","So when I plucked up the courage and approached him, he heard my sincerity.","Once, when Dr Bill Bassansky was in Kyiv, I decided to go and see him. I went to the hotel where he was staying with his team. When I met him, I introduced myself: «Dr Bill, my name is Dmytro Mason, and I am the pastor of a local church. Knowing your standing and influence, I still want to invite you to our church. There may not be as many of us there as you are used to.»","He replied: «You say there won't be many people? But will Jesus be there?»","I said: «Yes, He will.»","Then he said: «If Jesus will be there, then I'll be there too.»","From then on we became close friends. We were united not only by friendship but by working together on many projects.","It didn't matter to him how many people were in my church. What mattered to him was that Jesus would be present there. It was the true answer of a great man who understands that the real meaning of life lies not in material goods but in spiritual values.","This story reminds me how important it is not to be afraid to reach out to people, even if they seem out of reach. Courage, sincerity and faith are the keys to opening doors that may have seemed closed to us.","Don't be afraid to take the first step. You may receive far more than you expect. Truth, sincerity and courage always find a response in the hearts of truly great people.","«When the student is ready, the teacher will appear.» This simple truth shows how our world works. When we reach a certain level psychologically, spiritually or emotionally, we naturally draw to ourselves people, situations or opportunities that match that level.","If you change your inner values and your spiritual path, you will certainly meet people who share your beliefs, values and aspirations. You begin to «speak» the same language and understand each other almost without words. These are not chance meetings but the result of your inner evolution.","Yet when we face difficulties or failures, it is easy to blame the people or circumstances around us for everything. But the only way to real change lies within ourselves. Blaming others for our own problems is avoiding responsibility. A true student of life understands that every problem they face is an opportunity for personal growth and self-improvement.","Does our desire for growth and spiritual maturity mean we must stop spending time with people whose views differ from ours, or with those we cannot leave: friends, relatives or those who need our support? No, it doesn't.","First, it is worth remembering that true success is rooted in a big heart, in spirituality and in the true values the Bible calls us to. People who have achieved success always hold on to deep spiritual values.","Second, it is important to understand that being afraid of people with different views often points to one's own insecurity and immaturity. A true spiritual leader can engage with different people without fear of losing who they are. They joyfully serve others, whatever their beliefs, remembering the golden rule: «As ye would that men should do to you, do ye also to them likewise.»","Mature people have qualities such as humility and modesty, understanding that they are no better than others. They seek to serve, to share and to be open to the world, valuing each person's unique experience and path in life.","Life offers us many kinds of relationships, and sadly some of them can be harmful and toxic. That is why it is sometimes important to be able to set boundaries and protect your inner world from negative influence.","This applies especially to people who criticise constantly and without reason. Such people usually focus only on the dark side of life, absorbed in their negative outlook. We should also be careful with those who are always irritated or quick-tempered, since their anger can spread to others.","Mockers and scoffers, especially those who sneer at spiritual values, often do so because they see others through the lens of their own cynicism and distrust. People who are too pessimistic can infect those around them with negative beliefs that depress and dampen the mood.","So it is very important to try to keep away from such conversations. Negative company not only takes our precious time but can also leave a deep mark on our soul, affecting how we feel, think and respond emotionally. Remember that your spiritual well-being comes first, so always take care of your emotional surroundings.","There are moments in life when we have to make important decisions. Sometimes that means giving up familiar ties, surroundings or old habits that hold back our growth and spiritual development.","Remember Abraham. God gave him a great promise, but for it to be fulfilled Abraham had to take a decisive step: leave his surroundings, the land of his fathers, his customs and traditions. It was not just a physical move from one place to another but an inner change, a parting with the old and embracing of the new.","It is the same in our lives: sometimes we are surrounded by people or situations that hold us back, drag us down and stop us seeing further than we already see. These «surroundings» may be familiar and comfortable, but if they don't let us grow and move forward, an outer or inner challenge may await us, a prompting to change.","This doesn't mean we must abruptly cut ties and lose friends. But sometimes it is important to rethink the surroundings we are in and ask whether they really serve our best self. Each of us has a right to personal growth and a spiritual path, and if something is standing in the way, perhaps the time for change has come."],["Life is an ongoing drama in which we are actors, directors and audience all at once. Every day is a stage, every moment an episode, and every action part of a great script.","Life can be compared to a vast theatre where each of us is an actor. And each of us chooses which role to play, whether it has been assigned to us by fate or chosen by our own decision.","In childhood we play the role of daughter or son, discovering the world around us. In youth we are often searching for ourselves, sometimes playing the rebel, sometimes the student hungry for knowledge. As we grow up we take on the roles of parents, friends, lovers and professionals in our field. And these roles keep changing, because life never stands still.","But whatever role we have chosen, or whatever role circumstances have given us, the most important thing is to play it with respect for ourselves and others. To feel our own uniqueness, singularity and worth.","Some roles may seem less important or less visible. But even a small role can have a huge effect on the course of the play, just as in life. So every role we play deserves to be treated with all our devotion and heart.","But now a new test lies before us, a new stage in which we must learn to play the role of a new person. We have to learn new skills, gain new knowledge and overcome new challenges; all these stages are an essential part of self-improvement.","It is a role we have never played before, a path of self-discovery and self-fulfilment, in which we are to become a person who embodies success and becomes a living example that changing your life is possible whatever the circumstances. We will have to discover new horizons and opportunities and learn to see the world in a new way, from a new perspective.","It won't be easy, but every step, every small victory over ourselves, will bring us to a higher level of personal growth. We are learning not only to succeed in social and professional life but also to become better people who can influence the world around us and motivate and inspire others.","Changing your life is possible, and the process begins with faith in yourself, with the ability to see your potential and develop it. When we truly believe in ourselves and our abilities, we become an embodiment of hope and confidence for others, an example that the chance to change exists for everyone.","I still remember the experience that overturned my idea of acting and self-expression. Once I happened to accompany a famous actress, a star of stage and screen who was also a guest on various TV shows. We found ourselves in the office of a film company preparing to shoot a new series, and she was being offered one of the roles.","After the discussions and meetings, as we were leaving the building, one of the company staff called me back. In an office where preparations for filming were already in full swing, I was offered the chance to try out for one of the roles. I was surprised and at the same time touched by such an unexpected offer, and I agreed without a second thought.","While going over the details, they told me about my character's personality, motives and actions. I was to bring to life a rather dubious figure, far removed from my moral values. It was hard to imagine myself in such a role, but curiosity and the desire to try something new won out.","When I was asked to «get into character» and deliver a few lines in front of the camera, I felt very awkward. The words I had to say were so foreign and unlike me that I felt like a fish out of water. After the take I shared my feelings with the producers and said I was unsure about the role, because I couldn't see myself as a person so far from my principles and convictions.","Just as in film or theatre, in life we sometimes have to play roles that don't reflect our true nature. When we are forced to be someone we are not, or to embody others, it becomes a great challenge. It is hard to feel genuine when you are always playing notes that aren't yours. So when we try to play the role of a successful person living their dream, but deep in our hearts see ourselves differently, our «performance» may seem insincere and forced.","Trying to live out an image that doesn't match our inner «self» can lead to frustration and a sense of inadequacy. We may feel trapped in a role that confines us and quickly want to break free of its grip and return to our true nature.","Yes, expressing yourself in a new, «unfamiliar» role can be an important stage of self-discovery and personal growth, but only when the role fits harmoniously into your inner world and doesn't contradict your values and convictions. So every attempt to «play a role» should be grounded in self-knowledge and self-acceptance, in a desire to grow, not simply to «put on a mask». Then, perhaps, we can become the version of ourselves we see in our dreams without losing our uniqueness and authenticity.","Human beings are amazing creatures, gifted with the ability to live in two parallel dimensions at once. The first is our «real» world, where we carry out everyday tasks such as eating, drinking and working. This world is full of routine, measured by time and bound by its own physical laws and limits.","But alongside it there is another dimension: the world of imagination. In this world we can be anyone, do whatever we like and live in any time and place. It is a world where we can see ourselves on a mountaintop, flying through the sky or exploring the deepest oceans. It has no physical limits; other laws rule here, the laws of our imagination.","Interestingly, both these worlds are equally real to us. Our imagination can affect our emotional state just as much as events in real life. When we read a book or watch a film, we are carried into another world and feel the characters' emotions, even though physically we remain in our usual surroundings.","This unique human ability to dwell in both dimensions at once makes us special. It allows us not only to adapt to the outside world but also to create worlds of our own, where we find comfort, inspiration and new possibilities for self-expression.","Real change always begins from within. To become the person we dream of being, we must first form and live out that role in our inner world. It is important that this «new» role doesn't feel foreign or unnatural; instead we must take it to heart so fully that, while «playing» it, we feel it is not a game but our true self.","For a role to feel that natural, we need to dive deep into our thoughts, feelings and convictions. We must study and understand who we really are and who we want to become. We must allow our dreams, ideals and values to shape our inner «self», building new patterns of behaviour and thought that will become our new reality.","Such deep inner work takes time, self-knowledge and faith in yourself. It can be a challenge, but it is the only path to real and lasting change. When you become a true reflection of your deepest convictions and ideals, your «performance» will become your reality. You will feel that you are not «playing a role» but living your real life, expressing your true «self» in every action and every word. The very «role» you once felt to be invented or unnatural will become second nature, and you will be able to make your dreams come true without losing your authenticity.","In life, things rarely go according to a set plan or script. In many situations we face a choice without clear instructions or prompts. These are the moments when we need to let go of every doubt, take a deep breath and rely on our inner compass.","Improvisation is not simply trying to remember the «right» move in a given situation. It is the art of sensing the moment, the ability to perceive the world around us and respond to it with flexibility and inventiveness. Sometimes our improvisations lead to the brightest, most unforgettable moments of our lives.","So it is important to believe in yourself and your instincts. Even if at times we make mistakes, it is through them that we learn, grow and become stronger. Trust in yourself and faith in God let you face the unknown without fear, because you know that whatever the circumstances, you will always find an answer by listening to your inner voice. So when life becomes unpredictable, trust God and what He is saying in your heart. You are far more resourceful than you think.","Improvisation is not just spontaneity; it is an art form that opens limitless possibilities for invention, creativity and unconventional solutions. Every moment filled with improvisation has the potential to become a breakthrough, because it lets you find new, unusual ways of solving problems and bringing ideas to life.","Improvisation leads to the creation of something unique and original that can become a real discovery. It always contains an element of surprise and freedom, allowing us to go beyond the ordinary and traditional, to explore the unknown and to create the unrepeatable.","It is through improvisation that we can encounter new ideas, develop unknown directions and discover unknown worlds of possibility. It is the key to unlocking our inner world and the source of our creative energy.","Improvisation can become your constant companion in life, filling your days with unconventional solutions and creative ideas and helping you make breakthroughs and discover new horizons. Set your imagination free and give your ideas rein, and you will see the world around you transformed, filled with the colours and shapes of the unknown art of living.","Great actors always have a spark of creativity and the ability to improvise. This ability doesn't just make them artists; it makes them unforgettable in the eyes of the audience. Al Pacino is an excellent example of such an actor.","According to film-industry legend, during shooting he more than once asked the director for freedom to interpret the role rather than stick to the letter of the script. It wasn't a refusal to work on the text or a careless attitude to filming. It was his need to feel the character, let it into himself and allow himself to reveal it on screen as deeply as possible.","And as a rule it was these «improvised» takes that became special. They were full of emotion, sparks of living energy and an authenticity that made each of his roles unforgettable. This confirms that improvisation in acting is not simply a departure from the plan but a real way of revealing the depth of a character, of searching for its essence and its truth to life.","Dramatic turns are an unavoidable part of life, the cornerstones of our existence. Life writes its own scripts, in which highs and lows unfold before us a theatre of destiny that gives us priceless experience and new lessons.","In such moments, when we face the unknown and have to change course, we gain deep knowledge of ourselves and the world around us. Life's drama opens new horizons and paths, teaching us to rethink and to engage with the world at a new level.","The highs give us joy and dedication, filling us with energy and faith in ourselves. The lows, on the other hand, are trials that teach us resilience and courage, shape our character and help us grow spiritually.","Every dramatic turn is a new chapter in our story. They make our life deeper and richer and help us understand the world and our place in it. They allow us to grow, be transformed and mature, to set new goals and overcome the obstacles on the way to them.","Dramatic turns can be hard, but they always carry an opportunity for growth and self-definition. Through these trials we learn to treasure every moment, to rejoice in the instant and to discover new sides of who we are. They make our life unique, many-sided and certainly precious.","Every drama in life opens up an opportunity for reflection and spiritual growth. Yes, we will make mistakes, and sometimes we will wander or lose our way, but the key is to learn from those mistakes, because they too are an essential and important part of our life.","Mistakes are no reason for self-contempt or self-punishment. They are an opportunity, a chance to understand what could be done differently and better. They are steps that lead us to self-knowledge and an understanding of our weaknesses and strengths. They allow us to develop flexibility, resilience and wisdom so that we become better versions of ourselves.","Every mistake is a lesson that lets us see the world in a new way, to see different perspectives and paths. Living in a world where change is the only constant, we can keep learning, adapting and improving so as to move forward despite all difficulties and obstacles.","So instead of dwelling on our failures, it is important to accept and embrace our mistakes, draw valuable lessons from them and go on with new knowledge and convictions. It is this constant self-education and self-improvement that helps us build a life we are proud of and gives meaning to our daily journey.","Life often presents us with dramatic situations, but the key to keeping drama from becoming tragedy lies in our ability to keep inner peace. In stormy emotional moments we can easily lose control of the situation if we don't have a firm footing in inner harmony.","Meditating on the Word of God allows us to go deep into our soul and connect with God. It always becomes a beacon amid the chaos of our world. Through prayer and reflection we can find answers to many questions and receive guidance at the most important moments of life.","Fellowship with spiritual people who share our beliefs and values is also key. They can share their experience, give advice or simply listen. Sometimes it is exactly a word of support or advice from such a person that helps us see the right decision.","So to keep life's drama from turning into tragedy, we need to look after our inner world. Investing time in our spiritual life, finding a balance between the emotional and the spiritual and striving for harmony: this is the way to a calm, balanced life whatever the outward circumstances.","For me, the time I spend alone is especially important. These moments allow me to feel connected with myself. Reading the Bible helps me understand the teaching and principles on which I want to build my life. In prayer I talk with God, bringing Him my thoughts, feelings and desires.","It happens that amid the bustle of daily life and outward worries we lose touch with our inner self. So these moments of solitude are not only a way to relax but also a chance to listen to our heart, which shows us the right way best when we are in harmony and at peace.","I deeply believe that our heart is a compass in this world. And to hear it, we need to find a place and time for silence, away from noise and hurry. These moments of withdrawal are vital for me, because it is in them that I find myself and my calling in this world.","In life, as on stage, there are always spectators watching our every step and every role we play. These «spectators» may be our friends, colleagues, relatives or simply chance witnesses of our journey through life.","The feedback of these «spectators» is an important part of personal growth. Of course we would like to hear only positive feedback, but negative feedback is also necessary. It gives us the chance to see ourselves through others' eyes and to understand where we have succeeded and where we still need to work on ourselves.","By accepting feedback, whether positive or negative, we open up room for reflection and growth. It allows us to study our weak points, identify areas where we can improve and strengthen our strong points. Every piece of feedback is a chance to become a better version of ourselves.","Of course, not all feedback is objective and useful. But even in criticism you can find a grain of truth that will help you grow. As we live our lives and play our roles, it is important to be able to listen, analyse and, above all, learn. In this way, step by step, we can improve the scripts of our lives and become the main characters of our own dramas.","Life is a great drama in which each person plays their own unique role. Some of us, having suffered defeat or injustice, choose the role of loser or victim. Others, despite every obstacle, press stubbornly on, building themselves into the heroes of their own story.","But the most important thing on this great stage of life is not simply what we play. The main thing is being aware of and choosing the role we want to play. We are all actors on our own stage, but not everyone manages to understand that only we ourselves can decide in what light we will be presented to others.","Circumstances may sometimes push us towards certain roles, but it is always worth remembering that the only person who really decides who you will be is you. In choosing a role for ourselves, we also choose the path we will take and the face we want to answer for before ourselves and the world."],["Every one of us has at least once in our lives faced the task of shaking ketchup out of a glass bottle. The moment is full of tension and anticipation. You start shaking the bottle, hoping to add a little ketchup to your plate, but nothing happens. The ketchup seems to have decided to refuse its services and has set fast in its hiding place.","You keep trying: you tap the bottle gently, then start hitting it, but the ketchup only holds its ground more firmly. And then, when your patience is at its limit and you make one last desperate move, the ketchup suddenly bursts out, leaving your plate overflowing with red sauce.","This metaphor describes certain moments of our lives very aptly. Many times we put in effort, but the results seem small or invisible. We keep trying, hitting, pushing, but nothing changes. And just when we have almost lost hope, a breakthrough suddenly happens, and all our efforts bear fruit, sometimes even more than we expected.","Bifurcation (from Latin bifurcatio, a dividing into two branches) is a process of branching or a branching point. The term «bifurcation» is used in various sciences with different meanings, but it is usually connected with branching or splitting into two. In the theory of dynamical systems, a bifurcation occurs when a small change in a system's parameters leads to a radical change in its behaviour. For example, a stable state of the system may become unstable, or new stable states may appear.","Life is a continuous process in which any moment, any decision, can become decisive. Some people try to resist habit, change their fate and choose another path. But very often, despite all their efforts, it seems that no change comes.","Whole days, months, even years can pass in an intense struggle with our inner demons, old habits and stereotypes. We make the effort, do the exercises, read books, attend training courses, change our surroundings, but everything seems to stand still.","It might seem that all our efforts are in vain. But in reality something deeper is happening than we can see at first glance. Every action we take, every choice, every moment of reflection is a small step towards the decisive moment of our life: the bifurcation point.","The bifurcation point is the moment when all our previous work and effort begin to bear fruit. It is the moment when great changes start to happen swiftly, like an avalanche that has begun to roll down a mountain. And it is at this moment that we understand that all the earlier trials and challenges we faced were necessary to reach this critical point.","So when you feel your efforts are not bringing the result you want, when it seems you are banging your head against a wall, don't lose faith. Remember the bifurcation point. Perhaps you are already very close to it, and a single step could lead to swift, radical change in your life.","How many times in life do we face a situation where all our efforts seem to come to nothing, with no reaction and no response? You feel you have given everything, but nothing changes and there is no result. Isn't that so?","You know how much effort it takes to bring water to the boil. It has to reach 100 degrees Celsius for the water to change state. But what if you have been heating the water for a long time and spent plenty of energy, and still it isn't boiling: it is already at 99 degrees, and the water is still just water? What do you do at that moment? Give up the idea of a cup of tea and decide it was all a waste of time and effort?","We often feel we have reached a point where, it seems, only a little is left, yet we just can't reach what we want. It is exactly at such moments that it is important not to lose faith and hope. Perhaps only one step is left, one moment, one degree, and everything will change. The water will boil, and we can enjoy a fragrant cup of tea.","The system is waiting for its «bifurcation point», the moment when all the preconditions are in place and only one step remains for everything to change. Even when it seems that all efforts are in vain and nothing is happening, it is important to remember that every step and every action we take matters and has meaning.","Yes, it may seem to us that we have exhausted every possibility and nothing more depends on us. But I believe that every action, every attempt, every degree is a step towards a great victory, a great change. Even if it isn't always visible at first glance.","Life is not about giving up on the threshold of great change. It is about understanding that sometimes one more push, one more step, is needed for everything to turn out as you wanted. So when you feel the «system» is ready for change, don't stop. Perhaps all you need is to add one more degree of heat to see your efforts bring the result you want.","I really do understand what I am talking about. My own life experience has taught me that not all efforts bring quick results. Sometimes we put so much of ourselves into something, yet it feels as though nothing visible is changing. And that is when the demon of doubt appears in our head, slipping us thoughts that our efforts are pointless.","It begins whispering in our ear: «Look around, where's the change? Where's the result of your work? You thought you'd got rid of your old habits and become a different person. And here you are again, feeling something old that you tried to leave in the past come back and show itself in your behaviour, reactions or emotions.»","At such moments it is important to remember that the process of change is a long road that takes time and patience. It's like water in a kettle: it has to be heated for a long time before it boils. It is the same with us: even if you don't see quick changes, that doesn't mean they aren't happening.","So when doubt grips you again, when it seems once more that you have achieved nothing, take a deep breath, calm down and tell yourself: «It's all right, the water is still heating.» And keep going on your way, believing in yourself and your efforts.","There is a notion that the creative process is always accompanied by a spark of inspiration, that an artist always works under its influence. But this is far from the truth. Most great works were created through an endless process of trial and error, refining details and countless hours of routine work.","Yes, the initial inspiration can be an important catalyst, but it is only one stage of a long creative process. Many say that the first 90 per cent of the work seems easy, but the last 10 per cent requires the most strain, attempts and time. That 10 per cent is what separates a simple product from a masterpiece.","To become a master of your craft, you need patience and devotion to it. It takes great labour, countless repetitions and a lot of time. Sometimes the process can seem exhausting and dull. But it is through this routine process that a brilliant result can be achieved.","So when you feel you are losing inspiration or faith in your work, remember that the great masterpieces we admire were often created after countless hours of routine, invisible labour. Don't give in to the thought that your work is in vain. Keep going, and you will see your own masterpiece. The real masterpiece I am talking about is you! You are a work of the highest beauty and wisdom, created by the flawless Master, the Creator. Every detail of your being, your character, soul and body, fits a unique plan and design.","It is important to remember that forming your own character is co-creation. It is developing and improving yourself step by step, consciously shaping your thoughts, views and attitudes. It is an ongoing process of self-knowledge and self-improvement, in which we are both the craftsman and the material being worked.","To create your unique masterpiece, your unique self, you need to make an effort every day. Every action and every decision shapes your «self». It can be hard and take time, but every step forward brings you to your best version.","Work together with the Creator, let Him lead you, and follow the example of His unconditional love and wisdom. Trust the process and remember that every moment of your life matters. You are a masterpiece that never stops developing and improving. Believe in your strengths and abilities, and don't stop on the way to your original, unique «self».","Pay attention to details and to little things that seem insignificant at first glance. Sometimes it is these small elements that become the decisive drop that gets the ketchup moving out of the bottle, or the last degree needed for the water to boil.","Many people just want to «do something», believing that is enough to get the result they want. But the key to success often lies in the details. Superficial work or an unfinished project can look incomplete, just as underbaked bread doesn't taste right.","The thing is, when we create something, our imagination always adds the missing touches, completing the picture to how we want it to look. We see not only the real object but also how we want it to be, thanks to our inner vision. But our intentions and imagination are invisible to others. They see only what is in front of them: a concrete product or action without the hidden details. So always see your undertakings through to the end and give time to the small things; they may prove decisive for your success.","We are very often inclined to judge others by their actions and the results they have produced. But when it comes to ourselves, we tend to give weight to our intentions, rationalising our actions and results. This is a paradoxical side of our psychology that is important to understand and take into account.","Having good and ambitious intentions is undoubtedly very valuable. They become a stimulus that sets our inner mechanisms going and motivates us to act. But for these intentions to be genuine, they must turn into concrete steps, and those steps into real results.","It is not enough just to «want» or «plan» to do something. To achieve what you want, you need to spend effort, time and resources. Only then will our intentions begin to have a real effect, becoming action.","The bifurcation point in the context of personal transformation is not simply a moment of change but a critical point of transition, when a person's character passes from one state to another, bringing new opportunities and challenges with it. This moment represents a critical mass of effort invested in personal growth, effort that may have seemed small or insignificant at first glance but that in the end leads to sudden and perhaps radical changes in a person's life.","To reach this threshold of transformation, a person must keep working on themselves constantly and tirelessly, taking step after step on the path to improvement. Small daily efforts and actions that may seem pointless or insignificant in the short term can together, in the long term, lead to a deep and meaningful transformation of character.","Each of us has the potential for great change and achievement. It may take time, patience and faith in yourself and your strength, but every step, even the smallest, brings us closer to our own bifurcation moment, the point where we can experience a radical change in our life and being. So don't stop, don't lose faith, keep moving forward, and you will see your efforts bear fruit.","«Shall I bring some ketchup for your dish? Or perhaps I should put the kettle on?»","There are three reasons why we should not stop trying to make our lives more conscious and successful.","The first reason: God is our partner in creating life.","«Arise, and go down to the potter's house, and there I will cause thee to hear my words.","Then I went down to the potter's house, and, behold, he wrought a work on the wheels.","And the vessel that he made of clay was marred in the hand of the potter: so he made it again another vessel, as seemed good to the potter to make it.","Then the word of the LORD came to me, saying,","O house of Israel, cannot I do with you as this potter? saith the LORD. Behold, as the clay is in the potter's hand, so are ye in mine hand, O house of Israel.» Jeremiah 18:2–6.","God shows us that we are like clay in the Potter's hands. If our past attempts have failed, God is always ready to begin again, helping us reach our goals and carrying out His great plan. We should welcome Him into our lives as mentor and partner, so that together we create a true masterpiece.","The second reason: the need for constant work and sowing.","«In the morning sow thy seed, and in the evening withhold not thine hand: for thou knowest not whether shall prosper, either this or that, or whether they both shall be alike good.» Ecclesiastes 11:6.","The Bible calls us not to lose faith but to keep sowing seeds of goodness, knowledge and faith, because we cannot always see where and when a seed will sprout. We must believe that all our work will bear fruit.","The third reason: persistence in reaching our goals.","«And he said unto them, Which of you shall have a friend, and shall go unto him at midnight, and say unto him, Friend, lend me three loaves;","For a friend of mine in his journey is come to me, and I have nothing to set before him?","And he from within shall answer and say, Trouble me not: the door is now shut, and my children are with me in bed; I cannot rise and give thee.","I say unto you, Though he will not rise and give him, because he is his friend, yet because of his importunity he will rise and give him as many as he needeth.","And I say unto you, Ask, and it shall be given you; seek, and ye shall find; knock, and it shall be opened unto you.","For every one that asketh receiveth; and he that seeketh findeth; and to him that knocketh it shall be opened.» Luke 11:5–10.","This passage teaches us to be persistent in our prayers and desires. If we keep seeking, knocking and asking, we will find answers, help and success. Persistence and faith are the keys to fulfilling our dreams and desires.","Taken together, these three reasons teach us to work together with God and to be hard-working and persistent in our aspirations and desires. In this way we can grow and change our lives for the better, not resting on what we have achieved but moving forward with faith and hope."],["The help and support of others can be a balm for the soul, especially at times when life has brought us difficulties and trials. They can be a beacon in the darkness, showing the way and giving us strength to rethink and overcome life's obstacles. But such help must be well weighed and kept within limits.","We all long for the support of others, and we all have within us a need to help those who need it. Such interaction is a natural and necessary part of human nature. Yet there are situations where too much help can create a sense of dependence and inadequacy.","A person who becomes too dependent on others can lose faith in themselves and the ability to act on their own. They can become a hostage to others' expectations and live for the approval of those around them. Such excessive dependence on others' opinions can become a serious trap when a person needs to take important, personal and bold steps.","Dependence on others' approval can rob us of free will and the ability to follow our own convictions and ideals. Personal growth and self-fulfilment can be blocked when we live in constant expectation of outside confirmation instead of listening to our inner voice and intuition.","So help and support should always aim to strengthen the other person's independence and self-confidence, not to create dependence. Teaching and strengthening, not approval and holding back: this is what should lie at the heart of how we relate to and help one another. True help makes us feel our worth and our ability to choose, rather than keeping us in a state of powerlessness and dependence.","Sometimes life puts us in circumstances where it seems we are alone in our struggle with challenges and problems. At such moments, when we feel we desperately need support from others, we may feel especially vulnerable and powerless.","But it is in these very moments that a great blessing may be hidden. When there is no one beside us to «cover» or support us, we get a unique chance to prove to ourselves that we can cope on our own. Such moments often become turning points, when we take steps we would never before have dared to take.","It is in overcoming difficulties without outside support that we discover new sides of our abilities. What we do in such circumstances reflects our true potential, and the experience gained in such a struggle gives us a new level of self-confidence.","Face to face with challenges, we realise we are capable of far more than we ever imagined. And perhaps it is thanks to such moments of solitude and independence that we reach our greatest heights in life.","So if right now you feel a lack of support from others, don't take it as a punishment or a failure. Try to see in it an opportunity for personal growth and development. Use this time to gain experience, learn new skills and get to know yourself and the world around you more deeply.","Such times can be seen as a kind of «wilderness» that must be crossed to reach your promised land. The «wilderness» can be a trial, but it is also a place where we learn endurance, patience, faith and inner growth. It is a chance to take stock of our strength and realise that we are capable of more.","Perhaps it is in this «wilderness» that you will discover new horizons, find new strength and recover your inner compass, which will lead you to your promised land. Don't be afraid of being alone, don't be afraid of challenges and difficulties, because it is through them that we become stronger, wiser and ready to reach great heights.","Indeed, in the Bible's stories the crossing of the «wilderness» is a key moment on the way to the promised land or a blessed life. Everyone who moved towards a higher good met difficulties, trials and challenges that helped them become stronger and more enlightened.","This «wilderness» may look like a place of emptiness and lifelessness, but it is also a place of transformation and rebirth. Here a person has the chance to take hold of their faith, relying on God, and to find the strength within to come through the trials.","The main thing is not to stop and not to lose faith in the middle of this wilderness. The Bible's experience teaches us that it is important to keep moving forward, overcoming difficulties, with faith and hope in our hearts, ready to receive the best that God has prepared for us.","As we pass through our «wildernesses», with each step we become stronger and wiser, understand God's will better and become more ready to receive the promised blessings. So let your «wilderness» be not a place where you stop but the starting point of a new stage in your spiritual growth and blessed life.","There really are situations and trials that we must go through on our own. These moments are necessary for our personal and spiritual growth. When others solve our problems for us, we lose the chance to learn and grow through our own experience and put off our development indefinitely.","Every trial and every difficulty is an opportunity to gain new experience and new lessons. These lessons may be painful and hard, but they are what shape our character, our convictions and our view of the world.","So however hard it may be to overcome difficulties on our own, we must remember that every step forward taken alone is a step towards personal growth and self-fulfilment. And if we let others take these steps for us, we may lose valuable lessons and opportunities for self-improvement.","In the end, each of us makes our own path, and only through personal experience and growth can we reach our full destiny and discover our greatest possibilities.","Picture this: a butterfly tearing open its cocoon to spread its wings is doing hard work. It seems to be using its last strength, and you might want to help it by tearing the cocoon to make the transformation easier. But if we interfere and do that, the butterfly will not be able to fly and will eventually die.","It is this very struggle that the butterfly needs to live, because in overcoming these difficulties and trials it gains the strength and endurance it needs for the rest of its life. If we deprive it of the chance to struggle and learn, we deprive it of vital experience and condemn it to stay weak.","In the same way people need their struggles and trials in order to grow and become stronger. Each of our own «cocoons» is a trial we must overcome ourselves in order to grow strong and learn.","The Bible mentions a process of transformation, described by the term «metamorphosis». In the original language, the word «μεταμόρφωσις» (metamorphosis) describes a radical, all-round change or transformation, affecting not only outward appearance but inner being.","The word can be found, for example, in Romans 12:2:","«And be not conformed to this world: but be ye transformed by the renewing of your mind, that ye may prove what is that good, and acceptable, and perfect, will of God.»","In this verse «metamorphosis» means not simply change but a deep inner transformation that happens through the renewal of mind and spirit.","This process of metamorphosis in the Bible underlines the idea that a person can undergo a deep spiritual rebirth and change, becoming a new creation in Christ, throwing off the old and taking on the new. Such metamorphosis is not only a symbol of personal growth and development but a reflection of the divine image in a human being.","Yes, this process truly is personal for everyone, and no one can do it for us. So when we receive or give help, it is important to remember that when help is measured and limited, it aims not only to ease the way through obstacles but also to strengthen us and make us independent.","The aim is not to do everything for us but to help us learn how to cope better with life's challenges on our own. This matters, because each of us has our own path and our own lessons to learn, and each of us has a right to personal growth and development. Learning and growth come through experience, and experience often comes through trials and difficulties. So help should be the kind that allows us to grow and develop, not the kind that makes us dependent and passive.","There is indeed a great risk of unhealthy dependence, when other people's actions control us, or, conversely, when in helping others we try to control their lives, creating dependence. Too much help can lead to a loss of independence and initiative, because the person may start to feel they don't need to solve their own problems, and so in fact deepen their dependence on others.","When we become dependent on others' help and support, we may lose the ability to deal with life's challenges and problems on our own, gradually losing faith in ourselves. In this way our spiritual and personal growth can be stifled, taking us further from our main goals in life: self-fulfilment and inner transformation.","So every time we give or receive help, it is important to ask ourselves: «Is this help making me, or the other person, more independent and stronger, or is it just creating an illusion of support while causing dependence and passivity?» Reflecting on these questions will help ensure that our dealings with others are healthy and constructive, encouraging mutual growth and development.","Balanced independence really is a key to success. The process of metamorphosis happens inside us, and although others can support us, breathe faith into us and help us, they cannot walk this road for us. They cannot make the vital changes and adaptations needed for our inner growth and self-definition.","Each of us has our own inner world, our own challenges and experiences, and only we ourselves can do the important work of turning our fears, doubts and painful experiences into strength, wisdom and compassion. Others can only be supportive companions on this road, lending a hand and listening, but real transformation always happens from within us.","So in striving for growth and self-fulfilment it is important to keep a balance between independence and mutual support, between individuality and community, so that our relationships are a source of inspiration, strength and wisdom rather than dependence and limitation.","During trials and hardship it is very important to focus our efforts consciously not just on enduring or surviving the difficulties but on improving and growing. Every challenge can be an opportunity for growth if we see it as a chance to learn, adapt and become stronger.","We need to actively look for the lessons in the difficulties we go through, and to hold back the urge to retreat or avoid pain. We must remember that real growth often happens while we are going through pain and discomfort, and we can use these moments as a platform for building a stronger, wiser and more balanced self.","Trials can be hard, but they can also open new horizons and help reveal our hidden potential and talents. Instead of fearing or avoiding challenges, we should welcome them and use them as an opportunity for self-improvement and self-discovery.","«My brethren, count it all joy when ye fall into divers temptations;","Knowing this, that the trying of your faith worketh patience.","But let patience have her perfect work, that ye may be perfect and entire, wanting nothing.» James 1:2–4.","Think of the Gospel story of Jesus Christ. After it was publicly declared at His baptism that He is the Son of God, Christ went into the wilderness, where He spent a long time fasting and praying. At the end of that time He was tempted by Satan, who challenged Him: «Are You really the Son of God?»","«Then was Jesus led up of the Spirit into the wilderness to be tempted of the devil.","And when he had fasted forty days and forty nights, he was afterward an hungred.","And when the tempter came to him, he said, If thou be the Son of God…» Matthew 4:1–3.","And what exactly was this test aimed at, if Jesus had been called the Son of God from birth and this had been publicly proclaimed by John the Baptist? Because in times of trial and metamorphosis the question arises sharply: «Is this really me? Do I really have the right to what I am striving for?»","These moments of doubt and self-reflection are vital stages in the growth and transformation of every person. In these moments we, like Christ, must leave behind our doubts and fears in order to choose the path of faith and self-knowledge.","After His temptations and trials in the wilderness, Jesus came out in the power of the Spirit, formed and stronger.","«And Jesus returned in the power of the Spirit into Galilee.» Luke 4:14.","He held on to His identity and certainty in God, even when assailed by hostile forces. So it is important to find the courage to stand up for your identity, even when facing trials and temptations, and to come out of them in the power of the spirit, even more confident in your convictions and goals.","Set yourself on spiritual growth and transformation in such a way that every step you take, every action, every word and even your silence is filled with deep meaning and purpose. They should serve not only your own strengthening and growth but also become a source of positive change in those around you.","Every situation in life can become an opportunity for improvement and self-fulfilment. Even simple everyday actions can carry deep spiritual meaning if they are done with awareness and devotion. Your words can carry a power that inspires and unites, and your silence can become a space for inner self-examination and response."],["On the road to transformation we meet many challenges and obstacles, and one of the most hidden and destructive is the temptation of self-justification. This obstacle serves as a «safe harbour» for many who look for excuses for their failures and lack of success.","Self-justification appears when a person feels the need to explain away their inaction or lack of results. Phrases such as «I did everything I could» or «it's not up to me» show a lack of deep desire to change anything in one's life.","It is important to focus not on looking for excuses but on getting real results. Self-justification and refusing responsibility block our growth and spiritual development. We meet many people who present themselves as «victims» of circumstances, insisting they could have become someone else if it weren't for this or that obstacle.","Real change demands willpower, responsibility and determination from us. We must stop looking for excuses and take our lives into our own hands, understanding that every action, or failure to act, shapes our future. Giving up excuses opens the way to self-fulfilment and spiritual growth.","So why do we give in so easily to this illusion of self-justification? The answer is simple: the human psyche is wired to avoid pain, discomfort and risk. Effort, endurance and risk are the three main components of successful action, but they also bring a certain discomfort. So our brain sometimes looks for ways around them, offering an alternative route through self-justification and illusory action.","Such «clinging» to our own illusions can be very dangerous. It takes from us time we could spend on truly useful action, and energy that could strengthen us in our life's mission.","That is why it is important to understand that every illusion, every departure from our true goal, is a loss we inflict on ourselves. Instead of living in an imaginary world where everything always goes the way we want, we must set ourselves real goals, accept challenges and take risks as we move towards our dream.","Self-justification and self-betrayal are two sides of the same coin. They stop us growing and developing. So our task is to learn to see and understand our own departures from the path, accept them and change our attitude to them, so that we become stronger, wiser and more self-confident.","Self-pity and self-justification are, in my view, truly among the most dangerous enemies of growth and self-improvement. They are two elements that act as defence mechanisms, letting us avoid confronting our own failures, weaknesses and shortcomings.","Any of us, if we want to, can easily find «logical» reasons to justify the lack of change in our lives and to point to who or what is stopping us from succeeding. But all this is nothing other than a way of shifting our focus and distracting ourselves from our own responsibility.","Self-pity and self-justification are a kind of «drug» that temporarily eases discomfort and pain but sadly brings no real treatment or healing. They drain our energy and motivation, preventing us from moving forward and overcoming the difficulties on the road to personal growth.","It is important to learn to recognise and resist these mechanisms that kill growth, and to seek true healing and development rather than just temporary relief. Only then can we build a healthier, more fulfilled and mature life, with no room for self-deception and excuses.","There is only one way to your dream, one path that leads to it: an unwavering focus on action and results. Every step, every action, every result has meaning. And even if a result doesn't meet our expectations or is negative, it still matters a great deal. Because from it we can learn something new about ourselves, our path and our possibilities.","Every mistake, every failure, is not just a stone in the road; it is a stone you can stand on to climb higher. They teach us lessons and help us understand what needs to change or what to strive for. And perhaps most important, they give us the chance to grow spiritually and gain a deeper understanding of ourselves and the world around us.","Self-justification is a poor mentor from the very start of the road. That's because a person inclined to make excuses knows from the first step that they are not ready to overcome all the difficulties and trials on the way to the goal. Such a person may already have a ready-made script for failure, complete with detailed reasons and excuses for their inaction or failures.","This approach robs a person of faith in success and removes the motivation to act, since they are already convinced they will fail. Excuses pull us away from reality and make us focus on circumstances and outside factors instead of on our own actions, choices and opportunities.","Such a position is the self-destruction of potential and talent. It prevents a person from unlocking their abilities, opening new horizons and reaching their highest goals. So it is important to give up excuses and take responsibility for your life, decisions and actions, staying open to self-development and self-improvement.","The aim of self-justification is to protect one's «self» from negative feelings such as guilt or a sense of incompetence. Here are some of the typical features of self-justification.","Avoiding responsibility. A person who resorts to self-justification tries to shift responsibility for their actions onto circumstances, other people or vague outside factors.","How often we face the temptation to shift responsibility onto circumstances and outside factors. There are so many «buts» and «if onlys» that can always be used as excuses for what we haven't achieved. But our real interest does not lie in manufacturing excuses for why something wasn't done. The true measure is the result. And that result should be our main criterion, not the many excuses we can find for ourselves and others.","Distorting reality. A person may perceive events in a way that fits their expectations or desires, instead of seeing them as they really are. Distorting reality is when our inner images, expectations and wishes cover over the real circumstances and facts. We may look at the world through the «glasses» of our fears, predictions or hopes, and this distorts our perception. Instead of feeling and understanding reality in all its depth, we often see only what confirms the beliefs or attitudes we already hold. Such distorted perception can stop us drawing objective conclusions and making the right decisions.","People with a tendency to distort reality often use the phrase «it's not us, it's the world». This reflects a tendency to blame outside circumstances, society or other people for their own failures, blunders or conflicts. Because of this attitude they lose the ability to examine and improve themselves, convinced that the cause of all their problems lies outside them. Refusing responsibility and refusing to accept reality as it truly is leads to stagnation and stunted personal growth.","Minimising your mistakes. «Yes, I did it, but it isn't as bad as it might seem.»","Minimising your mistakes is a form of self-defence by which a person denies the significance or consequences of their actions, playing down their importance or effect. The phrase «Yes, I did it, but it isn't as bad as it might seem» is a typical example. By minimising, a person deflects responsibility, trying to convince themselves and others that the situation is not so serious, or that their actions were not as wrong as they might seem at first glance.","This kind of self-defence can lead to underestimating real problems and resolving conflicts wrongly. Blocking the chance to learn from your own mistakes hinders personal growth and self-improvement. A person who minimises their mistakes can get stuck in certain situations in life, unable to move forward and grow. So it is important to be honest with yourself, admit your mistakes and learn from them rather than play them down.","When we start looking within ourselves for reasons and explanations to justify why we didn't carry out some action or task, or when we refuse to take responsibility, we are in fact already giving in to the temptation of self-justification. Instead of looking for the answer to the question «How can I do this?», we choose ways of finding excuses for why we won't.","This becomes an obstacle on the road to fulfilling our dreams and goals. Instead of looking for ways to carry out our ideas and desires, we spend time and energy thinking about the reasons for our failure and inventing excuses for doing nothing.","The path of self-justification is a path of self-betrayal, on which a person loses the ability to see their opportunities and resources. It hinders growth and self-improvement, blocks inner potential and leads to stagnation and frustration instead of creative fulfilment.","To get past this barrier, it is important to stop looking for excuses and start acting, focusing on concrete actions and results rather than on circumstances or limits. Only in this way can you truly turn your dreams into reality and overcome the temptation of self-justification.","Self-justification and self-pity can indeed bring a certain pleasure, like the sympathy and pity of others. No wonder many people are ready to trade their dreams for «sweet» words: «I understand you; life really is hard, and people are often unfair.» Here I want to tell a hard truth that may not please everyone, but without which we may stay stuck at a dead point in our lives: give up self-pity, be demanding of yourself and don't look for sympathy from others. It may sound harsh, but it is better for people to envy you than to pity you. Better to be thought of as an ambitious person than as a victim of circumstances.","I understand this may seem cruel, but I am saying it only about how you treat yourself, your inner «self». Towards others we must always be kind and show love and gentleness.","Note that this doesn't mean disregarding your own emotions or feelings. It is about an active attitude to life, about taking responsibility for your own path and choices. It is about giving up the role of victim and taking up the role of creator of your own destiny. Only with this stance can you truly change your life and fulfil your dreams.","I am reminded of a story from the life of Smith Wigglesworth, a preacher well known in his day. When people asked him, «How are you feeling?», he would reply: «I don't ask myself how I feel; I tell myself how I ought to feel.»","This example shows the power of self-awareness and self-control. Wigglesworth believed in the power of words and thoughts, and his answer reflected a desire not to give in to negative emotions or sensations but to govern them, shaping his own experience and reality. Such an approach can help a person leave negativity behind and focus on the positive sides of life, which in turn leads to inner growth and development."],["When we think about a person's potential, we often picture some fixed measure or limit that can be reached. But is the limit of our potential really set by nature, or are we the ones who set our own limits?","Potential is the sum of possibilities that can be realised in the future. It is what a person can strive for as they grow and overcome obstacles.","When we reflect on our potential (if we really allow ourselves to), we often picture our abilities and define the limits of our gifts. But this self-assessment can be far from objective. First, we may not yet have fully uncovered our true abilities, so our judgements may be incomplete or distorted. Second, our conclusions are often based on past achievements and coloured by doubts and fears.","Our assessment of our own potential can be somewhat distorted by our own limits of perception and experience. We may underestimate our abilities because of past failures, or overestimate them while ignoring real limits.","A true understanding of your own potential comes not from comparing past successes or failures but from deep self-knowledge and devotion to self-development. We can keep learning, growing and improving, discovering new horizons and unexpected possibilities.","Potential is the sum of possibilities that can be realised in the future. It is what a person can strive for as they grow and overcome obstacles.","Human potential is dynamic and varied, and it can be at different stages of unfolding. The active phase of unfolding: here potential doesn't simply exist; it shows itself and grows through the actions, skills and abilities a person already recognises and actively uses. Recognised but unrealised potential: here a person has already recognised their potential but has not yet managed to unlock or realise it fully. Perhaps time, resources, knowledge or experience are still needed to unlock its full possibilities. Hidden potential: this is potential the person doesn't yet know about. It may stay undiscovered because of the unknown, self-imposed limits, fears or a lack of self-knowledge. To find out about this potential and unlock it, a person often needs to step out of their comfort zone, examine themselves and reflect.","Exploring and unlocking your own potential is an endless process of self-improvement. Each step on this path helps us learn more about ourselves, widen our possibilities and reach higher peaks in using our abilities.","We are often told that there are certain things we simply cannot achieve because of our background, age, education or other factors. But human history shows that such «impossible» things become possible through faith and our own potential. Indeed, people often say that «heroes appear precisely in hard times». This happens because in hard times people often find themselves in circumstances that require them to act unconventionally and go beyond their usual abilities and limits.","Such circumstances stir in people the need to show an inner strength, determination and resourcefulness they may never have suspected they had. Many of us live in comfort and routine, and only when we face difficulties do we begin to realise and unlock our true potential.","People no one imagined could become heroes are forced to discover new horizons of their abilities when the usual solutions stop working. They find in themselves a capacity for courage, self-sacrifice and determination that becomes key to overcoming challenges and difficulties.","Yes, hard times are often a catalyst for heroism and greatness of spirit, allowing individuals to understand and realise their vast inner potential.","But the real emphasis should not be on «hard times» or the circumstances around us, but on the fact that most of us truly don't realise what enormous potential is hidden within. What many heroes' stories have in common is not only that they arise in times of crisis but that these people discover in themselves abilities and qualities they never knew they had.","We often limit ourselves by our own ideas of what we are capable of. We form a picture of ourselves based on past experience, surroundings, education and upbringing. But every person has invisible reserves of strength, creativity and courage that can be unlocked when circumstances demand.","Our inner potential is a true source of possibilities waiting for its time to appear. We must believe in our abilities and develop the faith that we can overcome any difficulty, learn and grow, whatever challenges life sets before us. Then perhaps we will be able to unlock our potential not only in hard times but in everyday life too, doing amazing things and overcoming our limits.","Imagine that your life could unfold according to several scenarios.","The first scenario: you live in a world of doubts and excuses, and you do everything at a low level of effectiveness. Your life goes round in a circle of the ordinary, and you feel no need to grow.","The second scenario: you are active and try to be as productive as possible, but you are afraid to step into the unknown, into what is «impossible» for you. You reach certain peaks, and it seems to you that you are at the height of your abilities. Your life is full of activity, but you often avoid big challenges and changes.","The third scenario is the one in which you discover a completely new dimension and realise capacities you never even suspected. It is the road to a new level of personal and professional growth, the road to achieving what once seemed impossible.","Each of these scenarios has its own challenges and obstacles, but only in the third can you truly discover limitless possibilities within yourself, explore the unknown and overcome your limits.","The third scenario requires courage, faith in yourself, constant self-improvement and giving up excuses and limits. It is a path that lets us make our lives amazing and rich, where we can fulfil our dreams and aspirations even if they seem out of reach. Each of us can choose the scenario of our life. So which scenario have you chosen?","The scenario of lost opportunities, where you spend your time and energy on excuses, doubt and inaction? Where each day is a copy of the one before and there is no room for anything new or for growth?","The scenario of an ordinary life, where you do everything properly but don't allow yourself to dream big, don't go beyond your comfort zones and don't strive for more?","Or the scenario of a life of discovery and action, where you not only express your thoughts and desires more boldly but act decisively to make your dreams come true? Where you discover new horizons and limitless possibilities, overcome your limits and grow rapidly?","It is up to you what your life will be like. You can choose comfort and stability, but with them limitation and predictability. Or you can choose the path of self-improvement, self-fulfilment and discovering your true potential, a path full of new opportunities, challenges and discoveries. Which will you choose?","One of the most important factors in fulfilling your potential is faith. Believing that you can learn, adapt, grow and achieve what you want is the main step towards discovering your own limitless possibilities.","Faith is a powerful inner resource that gives a person the ability to see and sense things that have not yet appeared in the real world. It is a bridge between the inner world of thoughts, desires and convictions and the outer world of reality.","Faith is not just an optimistic wish or hope; it is a firm confidence that what you believe in already exists in your inner world and can become part of your outer world. It awakens in people the strength needed to turn dreams into reality and becomes the foundation for life-changing action.","Yes, faith is the conviction that something exists which has not yet become tangible but already lives in a person's heart and soul. It is faithfulness to your convictions and your own vision of the world, even when outward circumstances or other people doubt or deny it. And when we let faith into our lives, we open the door to new possibilities, creative self-expression and self-fulfilment.","«Now faith is the substance of things hoped for, the evidence of things not seen.» Hebrews 11:1.","I have always been struck by people who seem to have settled into the comfort of their habits, never allowing the thought that beyond the horizon of their understanding there may be an endless world of possibilities. They live as though everything is already behind them, not even trying to dip into the sea of their possibilities, let alone explore it fully.","This is not about judging or criticising; everyone has the right to choose their own path. But I am intrigued by the question: is a person satisfied with their life when they don't take a single step to discover the endless horizons of their potential?","It seems that the unexplored possibilities that could come from unlocking even part of their potential might motivate such people to open new worlds in their lives. Perhaps some are simply afraid of the unknown or of possible failure. Or perhaps some don't believe in their own strength, thinking everything is already decided and predetermined.","Life is a constant process of discovery. Every day offers new chances, new lessons, new adventures. I believe that searching for and unlocking your own potential can lead to a life filled with deeper meaning, joy and satisfaction. Because when we learn more about ourselves, we can live more thoughtfully and responsibly, contributing to the world around us.","I believe that every person has limitless potential that can be used throughout life in active searching and achievement. Interestingly, when we devote ourselves to a particular goal or task, we travel a certain path and gain the skills and knowledge we need. Once these skills and knowledge are mastered, we may feel comfortable working at that level, as if it were natural for us.","And it is right here that many people stop. From this point a person may think they have reached their peak and that all they can do now is improve within the limits of what they already know. Meanwhile, there is so much undiscovered that often stays out of sight. Perhaps out of fear of starting again, perhaps through a lack of faith in themselves, or simply from getting used to comfort.","It is important to understand that life is an unfinished process of discovery. By limiting ourselves, we lose the chance to discover something new, something that could change how we see the world, our possibilities and ourselves. So the choice is always ours: stay in the comfort zone or take the risk and discover the endless horizons of our own potential.","So I believe that for life always to be full of meaning, energy and new achievements, we must keep alive within us the desire for constant movement and activity. This is not only about physical movement but about mental activity, searching for new ideas and discovering the unknown. Such a stance keeps us from freezing in place or getting lost in routine; it lets us always be in process, moving towards new horizons. Every new day becomes a chance for new achievements and discoveries when the desire to live actively and grow burns in your heart.","Let me share some thoughts and advice on this. First, it is important not to be afraid of living in a new way. Remember how I said that «at every new level we seem to start all over again and learn to live in a new way»? In other words, a complete rebuilding of your life and character into something better and new is normal for an active person. Don't do something just because «that's how I've always done it».","A new path is a chance to discover new horizons and make your life richer and more interesting. We must not be afraid to give up the old habits, stereotypes and limits we have, and to step into the unknown with courage and faith, because that is often where the most interesting discoveries and opportunities await.","We should be open to the world, to new ideas, thoughts and people. We should keep learning, growing and striving for more. We all have enormous potential, and we should allow ourselves to realise it. So choose what will bring you joy and satisfaction, what will let you fulfil yourself and discover your talents and abilities, rather than what is considered «right» or «usual».","So let our lives be a constant process of discovery, searching and improvement, and may each of us find our own unique path to happiness and self-fulfilment.","Don't be afraid to be unlike everyone else, or to do things differently from everyone else. Want an example from life? Here's one: think about New Year celebrations. Visit any of your friends and you will see almost the same dishes on every table. It doesn't matter at all whether they actually like them; people do everything by the same script. And if you try to suggest something new, they'll ask you: «What do you mean, New Year without this? Everyone does it; what will people think of us?»","But what does it matter what others think, if it's your celebration, your table, your tastes and, in the end, your stomach? It is important to remember that your comfort and preferences matter and that you have the right to decide for yourself how to celebrate your holidays, whatever others say.","So be bold, be innovative, and don't be afraid to be different. The world is full of variety, and every person is unique. Don't lose your individuality trying to fit into other people's frames and standards. Your life, your rules!","Always seek to learn something new, even if it has nothing to do with your profession. Most people prefer to read books by like-minded authors, focusing on information that reflects their own point of view. So what new things do they learn? Right: nothing.","Read things that make your brain strain and require you to take in new information. In this way you will broaden your outlook, and this will help you see more possible options and ways of solving problems. Stay a student all your life. It might be new skills, professions or languages; it doesn't matter what exactly, as long as it inspires you to learn something new.","Discover the unknown, overcome the fear of the unknown, and you will see your world expand, filled with new knowledge and experience. Every day give yourself the chance to learn, grow and develop. This is the key to a successful and meaningful life.","«Let thy garments be always white; and let thy head lack no ointment. Live joyfully with the wife whom thou lovest all the days of the life of thy vanity, which he hath given thee under the sun, all the days of thy vanity: for that is thy portion in this life, and in thy labour which thou takest under the sun. Whatsoever thy hand findeth to do, do it with thy might; for there is no work, nor device, nor knowledge, nor wisdom, in the grave, whither thou goest.» Ecclesiastes 9:8–10.","It is no accident that the Bible calls us to dress so as to look attractive to ourselves and others, and to use fragrance. Why is this so important, you ask? Because such things help keep up your vitality and energy. When a person stops caring about their appearance, it often points to an inner decline and a loss of interest in life.","Taking care of yourself and your appearance not only reflects your inner state and self-respect but also affects how you feel and how others treat you. When we look well cared for and confident, it creates a positive impression, strengthens our self-confidence and can even open new opportunities for us.","So caring for your outward appearance is not only a sign of respect for yourself and others but also a way of keeping up inner well-being, vitality and harmony. It becomes a mirror of our inner world and a way of expressing our individuality.","The Bible truly draws our attention to deep feelings such as love and delight in life. People who are in love are usually happier and look more attractive. A soul that knows how to love is a healthy and fruitful soul. Such a soul radiates light, warmth and joy.","Don't let this power fade in you. Let your life be richer and more interesting than any film. Loving life is also our choice, our decision. Open your heart to love, not only for other people but for life itself and the world around us.","Some may not understand, but love for life is the guiding principle that helps us get through difficulties, rejoice in moments, find beauty in small things and so create happiness for ourselves and others. Love life, and life will repay you, filling your days with joy, happiness and meaning.","Become a rebel, in the good sense of the word, against stagnation, routine and the greyness of everyday life. Don't let circumstances and habits dictate how you live. Change your life; make it brighter, more interesting and more meaningful!","And now, attention: a bonus for those who have read this far! My signature phrase: «Turn your life into a celebration, not a necessity.»","Life can be a wonderful celebration, full of beauty, joy and wonder, but only when we ourselves choose to live that way. Life shouldn't be just a list of duties and necessities. It can be an adventure, a journey of discovery and incredible possibilities!","Be brave, be decisive, discover new horizons and turn each of your days into a celebration of life! Your life is your book, and only you can write it as the most gripping and impressive masterpiece!","So let's recall the words of an old song: «The revolution has a beginning; the revolution has no end.» Let our lives be constant movement and searching, with every moment filled with discovering the new and transforming the old. Let each day bring changes that lead to the birth of something new in us and around us.","Let's live a life with room not only for the known and familiar but for the unknown and new. Let our revolution of spirit and consciousness have no end but be an eternal process of discovery, learning and improvement.","Let's dare to set out on the path of unceasing growth and self-improvement. Life can be a thrilling journey full of amazing discoveries and adventures if we allow ourselves to be open, willing to take risks and ready for change.","May each of our days witness our inner growth and development, and may every thought and action be a step on the way to our highest potential. Let our lives be an endless stream of revolutionary energy and creative transformation!","And now I offer you the second part of this book. It begins with another saga, different from what you have read so far, but its essence only deepens the main idea of our story: the path of transformation."],["In the world of nature, where harmony and the richness of life prevail, there are animals that amaze us with their unique strength and devotion to life. Yet even the strongest of them are not spared great trials or moments of crisis. And it is in such times that they show their inner might and true purpose. Allow me to tell you the story of one such creature: the eagle.","The eagle is the king of the sky, ruler of the heights and a symbol of majesty. This bird not only captivates with its beauty but shows an astonishing resilience of spirit. Unlike most birds, the eagle does not choose the path of least resistance. It meets the storm, spreads its wings and flies into the wind.","What is special about the eagle is its unique capacity for self-renewal. Sometimes, feeling tired and limited in its abilities, it finds a shelter where it can rest and be renewed, a place where the sky touches the earth. In this refuge the eagle gives itself time to recover, reflect and heal.","And in this mysterious cave, withdrawn from outside challenges, the eagle finds the strength for inner renewal. Its body and spirit go through a process of metamorphosis that allows it once again to rise to new heights and overcome challenges.","We humans often face trials and difficulties. Like the eagle, we have the capacity to renew ourselves and adapt. These moments can become our time for withdrawal, self-examination and transformation. And just as the eagle soars into the sky again after its recovery, we too can find a new plan for life, turning problems into opportunities.","Allow yourself to regain your strength and find a new path, higher and further than every trial.","«Thy youth is renewed like the eagle's.» Psalm 103:5."],["In today's world we really do face a multitude of challenges, problems and stressful situations that can often lead to emotional burnout and a sense of inner emptiness. The circumstances of our lives can drain our strength, leaving us joyless and in despair. Having suffered losses and setbacks, we may feel crushed, disappointed and powerless.","Losing faith in ourselves and our abilities can be a great trial, making us doubt our strength and possibilities. We may feel confused, give up in the face of difficulties and feel uncertain about our future.","But even in this state of emptiness and burnout, it is important not to lose hope and faith in our own strength. It is important to remember that every crisis, every trial brings not only pain and suffering but also an opportunity for growth, recovery and self-improvement.","When we find ourselves completely empty, the challenge before us is to find the strength within, to discover a «second wind» and to rise higher than before the fall. It is a chance to rediscover the fire within, to deal with our fears and insecurity and to come out of the crisis stronger.","Life is often unpredictable, and sometimes reality can differ greatly from our plans and expectations. When we set ourselves to expect everything in our lives to go according to a predetermined plan and match our ideas and dreams, we become vulnerable to the disappointments and trials that may arise.","Some people take the collapse of their plans as the end of the world, feeling trapped and lost. The ruins of their hopes may seem insurmountable and the situation utterly hopeless. But it is important to realise that trials and unexpected obstacles are an inseparable part of life's road, part of the process of reaching a goal.","Trials can become important lessons and sources of personal growth. They can open new perspectives, opportunities and paths for self-improvement and self-fulfilment. When our plans and dreams fail, we must not lose faith but set ourselves to move positively forward, focusing on new dreams and goals.","Instead of seeing ruined plans as total failure, we should see in them an opportunity for new beginnings, for correcting our course and setting new priorities. This can help us become different, re-examine our lives and discover new horizons. When the inner world spins in a dance of uncertainty, and plans that were once the unshakable foundation of the future turn into sand slipping from under our feet, it is right here, amid the chaos and at what seems the imagined end, that we find a beginning. The beginning of a new turn of the spiral, a new era of personal growth and perhaps a new identity.","On the first page of this chapter, where in the inner silence only our doubts and fears echo, there is room for renewal. And it is not always an action or a planned strategy. Sometimes it is simply the act of being: allowing yourself to go through and feel what is there. Accepting that mistakes, failures and unexpected turns are not a sign of defeat but simply ingredients of personal transformation.","Recovery can begin with understanding that some things are beyond our control, that any dream or plan of ours may need to be rethought or perhaps transformed into something new. Here, in this space where we allow ourselves to be vulnerable and feel pain, we can find the seed from which a new state of being will grow.","During this metamorphosis, give yourself permission not to have all the answers and not to be sure of everything. It is in this not-knowing and uncertainty that we can discover new possibilities that were invisible to eyes that looked only at old plans and familiar roads.","And when we are renewed, when we start again, we learn to be grateful for what we have and for what we have learned. We may not lose our dreams, but we can learn to see them in a new light, open new paths for them and perhaps even let them be transformed along with us.","In the end, though our hearts may be weighed down by failure and disappointment, there is always room in them for new beginnings, new dreams and a new life that we can build even when the old is falling apart.","Every new day, every new opportunity, is a chance to be reborn and start again, exploring and appreciating the vast space of possibilities that opens before us when we learn to let go and allow the new to come in.","Holy Scripture contains amazing stories that reveal our human nature. One of the most gripping is the story of the prophet Elijah, which shows us that even the strongest in spirit can face emptiness and burnout.","Elijah was a true hero in the eyes of the people of Israel. His ability to stand up for the truth, his resolve in confronting kings and nobles, his direct contact with God: all this made him a legend. But even legends can feel weariness of spirit.","After the events on Mount Carmel, where Elijah showed the supremacy of the true God over false gods, he expected positive change. Instead he faced threats from Queen Jezebel. And although Elijah was a prophet and it seemed nothing could frighten him, he fled.","This was his time of desolation. A sense of rejection and helplessness, and perhaps a loss of faith in his calling. He wanted to die to put an end to his suffering. In the wilderness where he sought refuge, Elijah was at the very bottom of spiritual burnout.","But in this deep emptiness Elijah met God again. Not in the loud natural phenomena he had witnessed, but in a still, soft whisper of the wind.","God strengthened Elijah, fed him, gave him strength to continue on his way and renewed his calling. From that moment Elijah carried on his ministry with new strength, bringing God's will to the people.","This story teaches us that, however strong or called we may be, any of us can face emptiness and burnout. But it also shows that God is always near, ready to support us in the darkest moments of our lives.","«But he himself went a day's journey into the wilderness, and came and sat down under a juniper tree: and he requested for himself that he might die…» 1 Kings 19:4.","The true wonder and mystery of the human soul is that its strength can be so invincible at one moment and so fragile at another. The story of the prophet Elijah is an amazing example of this duality.","How could it be that Elijah, who stood alone against thousands, who unflinchingly opposed the priests of idols and openly challenged the king himself, was so afraid of one woman's threats that he asked to die? It was not simply fear for his life. It was inner desolation, a weariness of soul.","Every long struggle requires enormous inner resources. Even the strongest among us have their limits. Elijah's weariness came, no doubt, not only from unceasing outward trials but also from his inner struggle with himself, his doubts and fears.","After such an intense battle on Mount Carmel, where Elijah experienced an incredible triumph, he may have hoped to find peace. Instead he faced a new trial that turned out to be too heavy for him.","It seems strange, because somehow we imagine that after success comes a time of joy and rest. Yet in reality, significant achievements are often accompanied by a certain sense of loss. The goal that motivated us and drove us forward leaves a great emptiness in the soul once it is reached.","Why does this happen? Why does someone who strove for victory feel empty once the finishing tape has been crossed?","Perhaps the answer lies in the human spirit itself and how it perceives reality. Struggle, searching, overcoming obstacles: all this gives a sense of fullness and of the significance of our own existence. We pursue a goal, and this process becomes the very feeling of being alive.","But when the goal has been reached, we face the question: «What next?»","Sometimes victory can expose an emptiness that was hidden behind the curtain of our aspirations and ambitions. Our souls fix on our achievements and the smiling faces of the fans, and for a moment we may lose our bearings in our own feelings.","This reminds us how important it is to take care of our emotions and strength. We should learn not only to win but also to live through these moments of triumph wisely, sharing the joy of outward success while keeping our inner balance. The most important day is the day after the victory.","Victories and achievements are not the end point of our growth but only one of the stations on our road through life. They give us the chance to stop, look around and decide which way to go next and how to keep the fire burning in our soul.","Yes, this is exactly how God dealt with the prophet. He gave him time to recover and the chance to rest both physically and emotionally. After a period of rest and quiet, God set new goals before Elijah, goals able to revive his spirit and fill him with new energy, spurring him to move forward as a victor.","The new goals God set before Elijah not only gave him a new direction but became a source of new strength and faith in himself. Through these new tasks the prophet was able to find new meaning and purpose in his ministry, which strengthened his spirit and helped him overcome the inner obstacles he had faced after his time of victories.","In each of our lives there are times when we feel inner emptiness, desolation or burnout. It can happen after a long struggle to achieve some special dream or, on the other hand, after a brilliant and outstanding victory. In both cases the cause may be rooted deep in inner weariness, when soul and body no longer have the resources to keep moving forward.","The central feature of such moments is the loss of the main stimulus that kept us going: a goal. When we are working on a big project or pursuing a dream, our days are full of effort, energy and faith. But after the goal is reached, or if the dream does not come true, a vacuum may follow in which the familiar rhythm of life, the emotional load and the sense of purpose all disappear.","To get through such times, it is important to remember that this is a temporary state that can become a platform for new beginnings. Life always gives us new opportunities and challenges that can become a new goal, a new motivation to move forward. Inner burnout is not only a state of physical and emotional exhaustion. It is also a lack of enthusiasm, of faith in our own strength and, most importantly, of joy in life. Sometimes we are so focused on our goals and tasks that we don't notice we are giving away all our resources, leaving no room for recovery and joy.","As we spend our energy, we often forget the need to replenish our inner reserves regularly. Caring for our emotional and physical health and listening to our own needs and emotions matter not only during times of rest but also during periods of active work and pursuit of goals.","Look after yourself, set boundaries, find time for joy and rest, and do the things that fill you with energy and inspiration. Remember: your well-being is the key to being productive, creative and, above all, happy.","Remember that what may look like an end can actually become a new beginning. Life always offers us new opportunities and prospects, even when we face challenges or lose something important.","Moments that seem final are often turning points that open new roads and horizons before us. Every finished chapter of our life can become the first page of a new story waiting to be written.","See life's difficulties as an opportunity for growth and reflection. When a certain stage is over, you have a wonderful chance to turn the page and start a new chapter with new lessons, impressions and adventures.","In every ending lie several key elements of a new beginning: new lessons, new knowledge and new encounters. These elements can help you build a future even richer and more interesting than you could have imagined.","Keep in mind that you are always the author of your own story, and only you decide what words you will write on the next page. Your actions, your decisions, your strength and courage in shaping your own life: these are what make you the main character of your own story.","So don't be afraid of change; it is not always a sign of the end. More often it is a bridge to new opportunities waiting for you to discover them. Believe in yourself, work on your dreams and remember: every ending comes with a new beginning.","Thinking about how your life might have turned out, with the words «if only I had…», is a waste of time. Immersing yourself in thoughts of an alternative past not only steals precious moments of the present but can also drain your energy and motivation for the future.","First, you will never know exactly how your life would have developed with other decisions or circumstances. We cannot foresee all the variables and nuances of an alternative path.","Second, there is no way to turn back time and change the life scenarios already tried. Instead we have a precious gift: the ability to choose and to influence what is happening right now.","Focus your attention not on the opportunities lost in the past but on those you may lose in the future if you decide to stay depressed and burnt out. Soon you will realise that life holds countless precious moments worth your attention and experience right now.","Your time, energy and resources should be invested in the present moment and in planning the future. Investing in your well-being and prospects will bring more benefit than endless reflection on the «untravelled» roads of the past.","Besides, our past experiences, even if they were hard or painful, are already part of us. They help shape our convictions, values and character, becoming important guides for future decisions and actions.","Life is always worth living to the full: exploring, learning, loving and, in the end, growing through our own experiences and choices. Remember: your future path is always in your hands, and only you can decide what it will be.","And finally, the most important thing: not everything depends on you. Stop thinking that everything is under your control. Do everything you are able to do, and entrust the rest to God. He can bring incredible effort and resources to bear, help your plans come about and even surpass all your hopes. Try not to control everything or worry about every little thing. Put your cares and struggles into the hands of the Heavenly Father and let Him work in your life, giving you wisdom and strength when you need them most.","«Nay, in all these things we are more than conquerors through him that loved us.» Romans 8:37.","Life is not a rehearsal; what is happening to us now is reality. Even before we were born, the Creator already saw us as victors."]];